    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE REVIEWER A.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nSOCIAL SCIENCE\nLET REVIEWER UNIVERSITY\n1. The Sir Francis Drake Channel is located _______ the British Virgin Island.\nA. North\nB. South\nC. East\nD. Between\n2. What name was given by the Chinese merchants in the country during the early days?\nA. Xangley(s)\nB. Lhasa Tibet\nC. Guilin\nD. Silk market\n3. what is the famous Maranao bamboo dance?\nA. balse\nB. Singkil\nC. Kandingan\nD. kuraldal\n4. Known as the \"Lahar Region\" of the country\nA. SOCCSKSARGEN\nB. Northern Mindanao\nC. Ilocos Region\nD. Central Luzon\n5. The largest lake in the Philippines\nA. Iligan Bay\nB. San Pedro Bay\nC. Laguna de Bay\nD. Bacoor Bay\n6. Body of water that lies south of the Philippines\nA. Sibuyan Sea\nB. Samar Sea\nC. Celebes sea\nD. South China Sea\n7. The world smallest shell found in the Philippines\nA. Pisidium\nB. Tridacna Gigas\nC. Rafflesia arnoldii\nD. Hippocampus\n8. The places below the equator is in the _____hemisphere.\nA. Northern\nB. Southern\nC. Eastern\nD. Western\n9) the tobacco region of the country\nA. Bukidnon\nB. Cagayan Valley\nC. Cotabato\nD. Zamboanga del Norte\n10) the Philippines is almost as large as what European countries?\nA. Taiwan\nB. Italy\nC. Spain\nD. Greece\n9. The imaginary line which splits the earth in two halves is called the _________\nA. Hemisphere\nB. Equator\n\nC. Longitude\nD. Latitude\n10. The most useful indicator of the degree of democracy reached by a particular society is\nwhether it has a:\nA. Formal method whereby people can effect changes in\ngovernment policy\nB. System of government checks and balances\nC. Two-house legislature\nD. Civilian government\n11. The ancient name of Panay is ________.\nA. Aninipay\nB. Irong-Irong\nC. Baranas\nD. Aglipay\n12. President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo took her oath as President of the Philippines at?\nA. Malacañang Palace\nB. The EDSA Shrine\nC. The Quirino Grandstand\nD. Quezon City Reception House\n13. President known as the \"Savior of democracy\"\nA. Garcia\nB. Marcos\nC. C. Aquino\nD. Magsaysay\n14. An important document signed in Washington DC between the Philippine government headed\nby Magsaysay and the US on Dec 15, 1954 which provided for the gradual abolition of free\ntrade between the US and the Philippines from January 1, 1956 to July 3, 1974.\nA. Military Bases Agreement\nB. Laurel-Langley Agreement\nC. Exploring free trade agreement\nD. land use agreement\n15. The president of the United States is elected by the electoral college. What type of system is\nthis?\nA. Representative democracy\nB. Oligarchy\nC. Dictatorship\nD. Pure democracy\n16. In ancient Athens (Greece) tribes and generals took turns at power. This is an example of what\ntype of political system?\nA. Monarchy\nB. Dictatorship\nC. Pure democracy\nD. Oligarchy\n17. What type of political system is headed by Queen Elizabeth II of England?\nA. Monarchy\nB. Oligarchy\nC. Dictatorship\nD. Pure democracy\n18. total amount paid by Japan as reparation for the destruction committed by the Japanese forces\nin the Philippines during WWII\nA. $200,500,000.00 for 25 yrs.\nB. $200,000,000.00 for 25 yrs.\nC. $300,500,000.00 for 25 yrs.\nD. $300,000,000.00 for 25 yrs.\n19. Treaty signed by Pres. Magsaysay in San Francisco, USA on July 16, 1956 ratified by the\nsenate, thereby ending the state of war between Japan and Philippines\nA. San Francisco Treaty\nB. Penn treaty Park\nC. Treaty of Hubertusburg\nD. Treaty of Versailles\n\n20. The Zhou Dynasty claimed this principle gave them the right to rule.\nA. Mandate of Heaven\nB. Legalism\nC. Censors\nD. Shang Dynasty\n21. The two most important rivers in China\nA. Clang Hang & Hanfeizi\nB. Chang Jiang & Hanfeizi\nC. Confucius & Huang He\nD. Chang Jiang & Huang He\n22. The Great Wall of China was mostly built by _________.\nA. Labors\nB. Farmers\nC. Unskilled Workers\nD. Contractors\n23. In Chinese Society, the merchants were ranked below these ___________.\nA. Farmers & Aristocrats\nB. Farmers & Architects\nC. Foremen & Aristocrats\nD. Recruits & Originators\n24. Qin Shihuangdi based his rule on this is ___________.\nA. Permissible\nB. Legalism\nC. Endorsed\nD. Sanctioned\n25. Why did so many Chinese begin to practice Buddhism?\nA. Because the Chinese government required every person practice a religion and most\nChinese at that time did not have religion. Buddhism gave them peace.\nB. Because Buddhism allowed people to build hospitals for people and animals, built stupas,\nbuilt roads with rest stops and shade trees.\nC. Because parents wanted to send their children to the Theravada school of Sri Lanka which\nwas an early Buddhist schools that believed everyone was generally accepted as\nrepresentatives.\nD. Because lots of fighting and war broke out when the Han Dynasty fell and Buddhism\nhelped the people cope with their fear and stress. The Chinese were able to seek inner\npeace and cleanse themselves of worldly desires\n26. President from Bohol known to be a poet-politician and a good chess player.\nA. Diosdado Macapagal\nB. Carlos Garcia\nC. Ramon Magsaysay\nD. Manuel Roxas\n27. Who believed all humans were evil?\nA. Hanfeizi\nB. Confucius\nC. Liu Bang\nD. Laozi\n28. Who taught that people should put their family and community before their own wants?\nA. Hanfeizi\nB. Confucius\nC. Liu Bang\nD. Laozi\n29. Who was the founder of the Han Dynasty?\nA. Hanfeizi\nB. Confucius\nC. Liu Bang\nD. Laozi\n30. Who was the founder of Daoism and \"The Old Master\"?\nA. Hanfeizi\nB. Confucius",
