    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE REVIEWER B.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nSOCIAL SCIENCE\nLET REVIEWER UNIVERSITY\n1. Many revolutionaries were executed during the early years of the Katipunan. On March\n23,1897, Capiz witnessed the execution of katipuneros from kalibo. What were these martyrs\ncalled?\nA. \"Martyrs of Capiz\"\nB. \"Martyrs of Santo Tomas\"\nC. \"Nineteen martyrs of Kalibo\"\nD. \"The three martyrs\"\n2. The American consul-general who collaborated with Gen. Aguinaldo against Spain\nA. Adna Chaffee\nB. Manuel Tinio\nC. Spencer Patt\nD. Joseph Wheeler\n3. He vessel that Aguinaldo and his men upon their return to the Philippines from Hongkong\nA. Fort McHenry\nB. Victoria\nC. McCulloch\nD. Sampson\n4. The person who was named as 'Tiger of Mysore'\nA. Tippu Sultan\nB. Hyder Ali\nC. Sabdar Ali\nD. Fadek Hyder\n5. A Filipino sergeant who led about 200 Filipino soldiers and workers in the famous Cavity\nMutiny\nA. Paciano\nB. Gomez\nC. Zamora\nD. La Madrid\n6. 'Siravasthi' means\nA. Temple\nB. Town\nC. River\nD. Holy Book\n7. Which Ocean has one third of land surface in the world\nA. Indian Ocean\nB. Arctic Ocean\nC. Pacific Ocean\nD. Atlantic Ocean\n8. The science of constructing map is called\nA. Topography\nB. Demography\nC. Cartography\nD. Geography\n9. The Archbishop of Manila who defended the Filipino clergy even up to the execution of GOMBUR-ZA\nA. Archbishop Tagle\nB. Archbishop Martinez\nC. Archbishop Ledesma\nD. Archbishop Palma\n10. The Article which deals with 'Education for All'\nA. Article 41\nB. Article 43\nC. Article 45\nD. Article 44\n11. City where the novel El Filibusterismo was published\nA. Belin\n\nB. Kowloon\nC. Ghent\nD. Hamburg\n12. A satirical anti-friar novelette written by Graciano Lopez Jaena\nA. Fray Butod\nB. Diaryong Tagalog\nC. La Indolencia de los Filipinos\nD. Su Palan de Estudio\n13. Spanish Governor who SIGNED the death sentence of Jose Rizal?\nA. Gen. De Sande\nB. Gen. McArthur\nC. Gen. Polavieja\nD. Gen. Despujol\n14. Who is known as the Father of Economics\nA. Karl Marx\nB. John Marshall\nC. Malthus\nD. Adam Smith\n15. 'Khajuraho' temple was built by\nA. Sandelas\nB. Chauhans\nC. Prathiharas\nD. Rajputs\n16. Which is the nearest planet to the sun in the solar system?\nA. Earth\nB. Marse\nC. Mercury\nD. Jupiter\n17. Choose the largest map scale from the following\nA. 1:50,000\nB. 1:00,000\nC. 1:250,000\nD. None of these\n18. Spanish Governor who ordered the DEPORTATION of Jose rizal to Dapitan is\nA. Gen. De Sande\nB. Gen. McArthur\nC. Gen. Polavieja\nD. Gen. Despujol\n19. Date of proclamation of the first Philippines Republic\nA. June 12, 1894\nB. July 4, 1946\nC. June 4, 1894\nD. July 12, 1946\n20. The basic features of Economics are\nA. Production, Labor, Income\nB. Production, Labor, Consumption\nC. Production, Distribution, Income\nD. Production, Distribution, Consumption\n21. The King who invaded India many a times to capture Punjab before the third Battle of Panipet\nA. Mohamud Ghori\nB. Auranzeb\nC. Ahamed Shah Abdali\nD. Gazani Mohamud\n22. The Atmospheric layer responsible for weather changes\nA. Stratosphere\nB. Troposphere\nC. Ionosphere\nD. Exosphere\n23. Event which mark the fall of the first Philippine Republic.\nA. Cadiz Constitution is rejected by the conservative government and Filipino representation in\n\nthe Spanish Cortes is abolished.\nB. Deaths of Jose Rizal\nC. Pedro Bravo de Acuña appointed Governor-General\nD. Capture of Aguinaldo\n24. What island was Napoleon born on?\nA. Elba\nB. Corsica\nC. Saint Helena\nD. Outer Hebrides\n25. Who commanded the Prussian forces at Waterloo?\nA. The Duke of Wellington\nB. Mr Wilson\nC. Gebhard Blucher\nD. Frederick William III\n26. Iconography was introduced by\nA. Cholas\nB. Later Cholas\nC. Pallavas\nD. Later Pallavas\n27. The Father of History\nA. Lyxes\nB. Herodutos\nC. Cyrus\nD. Halikarnassos\n28. The first American newspaper to be published in the Philippines\nA. Bounding Billow\nB. Newsday\nC. The Baltimore Sun\nD. The Liberator\n29. The right to property is-\nA. All of these\nB. A fundamental right\nC. A citizen's right\nD. A legal right\n30. A teacher has to be adapted at-\nA. Acting\nB. Learning\nC. Communication\nD. Playing multiple roles\n31. The Fundamental Rights in India are designed to-\nA. Ensure rights of human beings\nB. ensure that all Indians can lead their lives in peace and harmony as citizens of\nIndia\nC. protect liberty\nD. protect freedom\n32. Part of the complexity in teaching social sciences lies in the fact that their subjects is-\nA. Every changing\nB. Very complex\nC. Non-existent\nD. Localized\n33. When does history begin?\nA. when human civilization begins\nB. when human memory begins\nC. when written sources be-come available\nD. All of these\n34. The first Japanese General to land in the Philippines\nA. Douglas MacArthur\nB. Shizuichi Tanaka\nC. Tomoyuki Yamashita\nD. General Masaharu Homma",
