    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE REVIEWER B.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n35. Which of the following occupies the largest cultivated area in India-\nA. Barley and maize\nB. Jowar and bajra\nC. Wheat\nD. Rice\n36. The chief organ of the Japanese propaganda\nA. KALIBAPI\nB. KALAPATI\nC. KAPISANAN\nD. KUMAJA\n37. What was Benevolent Assimilation?\nA. American efforts to make the Philippines more Spanish\nB. American efforts to grant the island their independence immediately\nC. Filipino efforts to gain the goodwill of the Americans\nD. American efforts to provide for the Philippines until a suitable leader was found\n38. In terms of history which is the proper chronological order-\nA. Paleolithic, Megalithic, Microlithic, Neolithic\nB. Neolithic, Megalithic, Paleolithic, Microlithic\nC. Paleolithic, Neolithic, Microlithic, Megalithic\nD. Microlithic, Neolithic, Megalithic, Paleolithic\n39. The greatest impact on the environment of earth has been from-\nA. Atomic blasts\nB. Human activity\nC. Chemical pollution\nD. Solar radiation\n40. Where rice was first domesticated?\nA. Antarctica\nB. South Asia\nC. America\nD. Europe\n41. The location of Fertile Crescent refers to:\nA. The yellow river basin, China.\nB. Two river basins, ancient Babylon.\nC. The Nile basin, ancient Egypt.\nD. Silmugi River, borbon\n42. Which famous code is the sentence \"An eye for an eye. A tooth for a tooth.\" from?\nA. Hammurabi Code\nB. Law of the Twelve Tables\nC. Elements of International Law\nD. Justinian Codes\n43. The third planet in the solar system is also called-\nA. Venus\nB. Mars\nC. Earth\nD. Mercury\n44. The last emperor of the Roman Republic, also the first emperor of the Roman Empire, the one\nwho quelled the civil strife of the Republic, the one who established the emperor of the Roman\nEmpire is:\nA. Gayves House Dawei Augustus\nB. Nero Claudius\nC. Gayus Urius Caesar\nD. Marcus Aurelius\n45. Ashoka's dhamma was-\nA. A principle of good conduct\nB. An ideology\nC. A set of ideas propagated by emperor Ashoka\nD. All of the these\n46. In the legend of King Arthur, the knights of the round table united the British Isles. One of the\nknights, who was also a bastard of Arthur betrayed the King, and died with Arthur in the battle\nof Karman. The name of this knight was:\n\nA. Gawain\nB. Lancelot\nC. Mordred\nD. Queen Guinevere\n47. The science that deals with the study of the Earth and its lands, features, inhabitants, and\nphenomena is called-\nA. Paleontology\nB. Geography\nC. Biology\nD. Sociology\n48. Where the mind is without fear\" were lines by-\nA. Mahatma Gandhi\nB. Swami Vivekananda\nC. Gurudev Rabindranath Tagore\nD. Sardar Bhagat Singh\n49. What was the name of the first manned spacecraft to land on the moon?\nA. Eagle\nB. Columbia\nC. Gumdrop\nD. Enterprise\n50. Dateline: 15 March, 44 B.C. - What significant event happened on this date?\nA. Death of Pope Lucius II\nB. Columbus returns to Spain from America\nC. Assassination of Julius Caesar\nD. Andrew Jackson born",
