    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE REVIEWER C.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nSOCIAL SCIENCE\nLET REVIEWER UNIVERSITY\n1. In the history of the ancient Indian peacock dynasty, the third emperor, known as the king of\nBuddhism is:\nA. Chandragupta Maurya\nB. Ashoka\nC. Samudragupta\nD. Dasharatha\n2. What is the oldest epic in the history of mankind?\nA. Mahabharata（India）\nB. Gilgamesh Epic（Babylon)\nC. Homer's epic（Ancient Greece）\nD. Toldi's Eve (England)\n3. The civil war of which country lasted from 1936-1939?\nA. Spain\nB. Portugal\nC. Greece\nD. Lithuania\n4. Who established Pennsylvania?\nA. Benjamin Franklin\nB. William Penn\nC. John Hancock\nD. Bumblebee\n5. What is the fiery name given to the famous Civil War General Sherman's military tactics?\nA. Scorched earth\nB. Vertical envelopment\nC. Massed howitzer fire\nD. Pride's purge\n6. The name of a dynasty with the longest duration in human history is:\nA. Byzantine Dynasty\nB. Zhou Dynasty\nC. Tudor Dynasty\nD. Tang Dynasty\n7. What prominent Greek orator overcame a speech handicap by putting stones in his mouth?\nA. Phaeax\nB. Aristogeiton\nC. Demosthenes\nD. Androtion\n8. The ancient South American civilization located in the south of South America today, stretching\nfrom central Ecuador to central Chile is:\nA. Aztec\nB. Maya\nC. Applied\nD. Inca\n9. What grand-nephew of Julius Caesar was the first emperor of Rome?\nA. Augustus\nB. Mark Antony\nC. Pompey\nD. Ajax the Lesser\n10. Launched in 1973, what was the first space station owned and operated by NASA?\nA. Skylab\nB. Salyut\nC. Mir\nD. International Space Station\n11. By which name was the American World War 2 Medium tank 'M4' better known?\nA. Pershing\nB. Grant\n\nC. Sherman\nD. Tiger\n12. The capital of the Ottoman Empire is Istanbul, and during the Roman Empire it was named\nafter a famous emperor, which was:\nA. Claudius\nB. Constantinople\nC. Justinian Fort\nD. Ottoman\n13. During WWII, what does the term 'ghost division' generally mean?\nA. a division that only existed on paper\nB. a division that had been destroyed\nC. a division that had not deployed yet\n14. \"The Old Dominion State\" is the official nickname of which U.S. state?\nA. Louisiana\nB. Virginia\nC. Oregon\nD. Ohio\n15. What nation has the longest border with the U.S.?\nA. England\nB. Canada\nC. Mexico\nD. Sudan\n16. Which country in Europe is also known as 'The Boot'?\nA. Italy\nB. France\nC. Portugal\nD. Spain\n17. Which country, the capital city of which is Cairo, is also known as 'Om El Donya'?\nA. Iraq\nB. Iran\nC. Egypt\nD. Somalia\n18. What city has been dubbed the Chocolate Capital of the United States?\nA. Hershey\nB. Carmel\nC. Cocoa\nD. Ding Dong\n19. 'Old Blighty' is the nickname of which European country?\nA. Italy\nB. France\nC. Spain\nD. United Kingdom\n20. Finland is also known by what name?\nA. The Land of a Thousand Lakes\nB. The Land of the Rising Sun\nC. The land of Poets\nD. The Land of Blue Skies\n21. Which country is also referred to as 'Hellas'?\nA. Turkey\nB. Greece\nC. Albania\nD. Bulgaria\n22. Which country, that was once known as Ceylon, has also been referred to as 'Zeilan'?\nA. Oman\nB. Somalia\nC. Yemen\nD. Sri Lanka\n23. In which ocean would you find the island of Guam?\nA. Pacific Ocean\nB. Atlantic Ocean\n\nC. Indian Ocean\nD. Arctic Ocean\n24. Who was the first Pole to become a Pope?\nA. Karol Wojtyla\nB. Lech Walesa\nC. Zbigniew Boniek\nD. Henryk Sienkiewicz\n25. What is the other for the Philippines Autonomy Act of 1916?\nA. Jones Law\nB. Tyding Mcduffie act\nC. Hare-Hawes Cutting Act\nD. Treaty of Paris\n26. Where is the Temple of the Tooth found?\nA. India\nB. Thailand\nC. France\nD. Sri Lanka\n27. The highest mountain in Iran is:\nA. Mount Everest\nB. Pamir Mountain\nC. Mount Damavand\nD. Lenin Peak\n28. Who wrote the \"Kartilla\", considered the 'bible' of the Katipunan movement?\nA. Emilio Jacinto\nB. Andres Bonifacio\nC. Apolinario Mabini\nD. Valentin Diaz\n29. Who created the designs for the Philippine national flag?\nA. Marcela Agoncillo\nB. Julian Felipe\nC. Apolinario Mabini\nD. Emilio Aguinaldo\n30. Who named the country 'Islas de San Lazaro'?\nA. Ferdinand Magellan\nB. Diego Barbosa\nC. Miguel Lopez de Legazpi\nD. Alvaro Saavedra\n31. Who was the first Filipino recording artist?\nA. Imelda Papin\nB. Pilita Corales\nC. Margi Moran\nD. Maria Carpena\n32. Who founded the la Liga Filipina?\nA. Jose Rizal\nB. Emilio Jacinto\nC. Andres Bonifacio\nD. Emilio Aguinaldo\n33. What is the first word of the 1987 Philippine Constitution?\nA. I\nB. People\nC. The\nD. We\n34. Who was the first Miss Philippines?\nA. Margi Moran\nB. Mirriam Quiambao\nC. Evangeline Castro\nD. Gloria Diaz\n35. Who was the first Filipino Olympian?\nA. Paeng Nepomuceno\nB. Efren 'Bata' Reyes\n\nC. Akiko Thompson\nD. David Nepomuceno\n36. Whose last words were 'It is done!'\nA. Ninoy Aquino\nB. Jose Rizal\nC. Manuel Quezon\nD. Andres Bonifacio\n37. Who designed the Rizal Monument?\nA. Antonio Luna\nB. Carlos Nicoli\nC. Richard Kissling\nD. David Antel\n38. In 1908, the Philippines Premier State University was created by Act No. 1870. Name the\nuniversity______\nA. University of the Philippines\nB. University of Sto. Tomas\nC. Escuela Municipal de Manila\nD. De La Salle University\n39. He arrived in Cebu in 1565 to establish the first Spanish settlement in the Philippines, marking\nthe beginning of Spain's colonization and Christianization of the archipelago. Who was he?\nA. Ferdinand Magellan\nB. Christopher Columbus\nC. Antonio Pigafetta\nD. Miguel Lopez de Legazpi\n40. In 1851, the first commercial bank in the Philippines and the far East, was established. What is\nthe present name of this bank?\nA. Bangko Central ng Pilipinas\nB. Bank of the Philippine Islands\nC. Banco de las islas Filipinas\nD. Far East bank\n41. After the death of her husband Andres Bonifacio, Gregoria de Jesus was later married to\nwhom?\nA. Julio Nakpil\nB. Jose Calugas\nC. Felipe Calderon\n42. Who was the last Sultan of Sulu?\nA. Haji Butu\nB. Tarhata Kiram\nC. Abu Bakr\nD. Jamalul Kiram II\n43. The first woman to top the Philippine BAR Examination.\nA. Tecla San Andres Ziga\nB. Tina Munoz Palma\nC. Josefa Diokno\nD. Geronima Pecson\n44. He was also known as Hermano Pule.\nA. Aurelio Tolentino\nB. Apolinario de la Cruz\nC. Juan Arellano\nD. Pedro Feced\n45. Who was the chief advisor of Gen. Emilio Aguinaldo?\nA. Pedro Paterno\nB. Jose Rizal\nC. Felipe Calderon\nD. Apolinario Mabini\n46. The first political party in the Philippines organized on December 23, 1900 by wealthy Filipino\nillustrados.\nA. Partido Nacional Progresibo\nB. Nacionalista Party",
