    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE REVIEWER E.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nSOCIAL SCIENCE\nLET REVIEWER UNIVERSITY\n1. It is characterized by shared experiences and mutual responsibilities.\na. Gesellschaft\nb. Gemeinschaft\nc. Enculturation\nd. Acculturation\n2. It features the exchange of goods, money and services.\na. Gesellschaft\nb. Gemeinschaft\nc. Enculturation\nd. Acculturation\n3. The longest revolt in the Philippine History is called the ______.\na. Dagohoy revolt\nb. Diego Silang revolt\nc. Gabriela Silang revolt\nd. Palaris revolt\n4. Violation of human rights is a violation of the _____ of persons.\na. dignity\nb. intelligence\nc. emotions\nd. freedom\n5. The “yellow race “is also known as:\na. Caucasians\nb. Mongoloids\nc. Negros’s\nd. Malays\n6. The highest mountain in the continent of Africa is ______.\na. Mt. Everest\nb. Mt. Kilimanjaro\nc. Mt. Fuji\nd. Mt. Apo\n7. In this poem, Rizal noted the role of religion in attaining good education.\na. Remembrance to my Hometown\nb. Our Mother Tongue\nc. To Education\nd. Intimate alliance between religion and good education\n8. Martial law remained in force until 1981 under Proclamation # ______.\na. 1081\nb. 1425\nc. 9994\nd. 7610\n9. The process by which a person learns the requirements of the culture by which he or she\nis surrounded, and acquires values and behaviors that are appropriate or necessary in\nthat culture is called ______.\na. assimilation\nb. enculturation\nc. cultural relativism\nd. acculturation\n10. The difference between gross profit and cost of goods sold is known as ______.\na. markdown\nb. discount\nc. net profit\nd. invoice price\n11. The Philippines lies in the region where many volcanoes are active. This region is known\nas _____.\na. Wheel of Fire\nb. Ring of fire\n\nc. Volcanic Rim\nd. Archipelagic Fault Line\n12. I have but one life to give and I am willing to give it to my country, not everyone is given\nthis chance. Justice Abad Santos answered the Japanese soldiers. This finds an\nequivalent in valor of _________.\na. Jose Rizal\nb. Marcelo del Pilar\nc. President Aquino\nd. Governor Aguinaldo\n13. The exchange of cultural features that results when groups of individuals from different\ncultures come into continuous first-hand contact. The original cultural patterns of either or\nboth groups may be altered, but the groups remain distinct.\na. assimilation\nb. enculturation\nc. cultural relativism\nd. acculturation\n14. The commander of the American and Filipino forces in Bataan was ______\na. Gen. Arthur MacArthur\nb. Gen. Douglas MacArthur\nc. Gen. Jonathan Wainwrights\nd. Gen. Edward P. King\n15. The first American Civil Governor was ______.\na. William Howard Taft\nb. Wesley Merritt\nc. Arthur MacArthur\nd. Murray\n16. The function by which schools help children to participate effectively in larger society is\ncalled:\na. Socialization\nb. Education\nc. Enculturation\nd. Acculturation\n17. Kmono ______ kilt Scandinavian\na. Indian\nb. Indonesian\nc. Chinese\nd. Japanese\n18. King of beats lion king of birds _______.\na. robin\nb. sparrow\nc. eagle\nd. falcon\n19. Jewish kosher halal\na. Muslim\nb. Buddhist\nc. Christian\nd. Pagans\n20. Catholic priest Buddhist ______\na. Imam\nb. rabbi\nc. lama\nd. pope\n21. Laity lay people clergy ______\na. clergymen\nb. clerics\nc. clergy\nd. clerks\n22. What is the foundation of genuine peace and reconciliation?\na. Joy\n\nb. Confrontation\nc. happiness\nd. Social justice\n23. What was our government under the 1935 constitution?\na. Revolutionary\nb. Monarchy\nc. Commonwealth\nd. Military\n24. What values are being promoted by the Philippine Government when it launched the “Juan\nTime” project in 2011?\na. Punctuality\nb. Austerity\nc. Palabra de Honor\nd. Close family ties\n25. If you seeing your ways of doing things as the right way and everybody else`s as the\nwrong way, you tend to have the attitude called ____________.\na. Cultural relativism\nb. Ethical relativism\nc. Ethnocentrism\nd. Xenophobia\n26. It refers to any liability to pay money arising out of a contract, express or implied.\na. Poll tax\nb. Tax\nc. Debt\nd. Debtors\n27. He coined the term “survival of the fittest.”\na. August Comte\nb. Karl Marx\nc. Herbert Spencer\nd. Arnold Toynbee\n28. In whose presidency was the famous miracle rice produced?\na. Ferdinand Marcos\nb. Fidel Ramos\nc. Joseph Estrada\nd. Sergio Osmena\n29. In Economics, __________ is the rise in the general level of prices of goods and services\nin an economy a period of time.\na. Inflation\nb. mercantilism\nc. depression\nd. free trade\n30. 150. Which of the following best describes the science of Ecology?\na. Living things\nb. Rocks\nc. Life and environment\nd. Weather and climate\n31. This court shall have jurisdiction over civil and criminal case involving graft and corrupt\npractices and such offenses committed by public officers and employees in relation to\ntheir offices as may be determined by law.\na. Court of Appeals\nb. Regional Trial Courts\nc. Sandiganbayan\nd. Supreme Court\n32. This was a prize winning-poem of Rizal when he was a student in UST. This poem proved\nthat an Indio was not only equal but also more superior than the Spaniards in poetry\nwriting.\na. To the Filipino Youth\nb. They ask Me for Verses\nc. Hymn to Talisay\nd. Kundiman",
