    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE REVIEWER J.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nb. 4 3 2 5 1\nc. 2 3 4 1 5\nd. 1 4 5 2 3\nBased on the early historical accounts of Europe these two nations had strong ties with\nthe European culture and the Asian nations.\na. Australia and New Zealand\nb. India and Sri Lanka\nc. Turkey and Russia\nd. Iran and Iraq\nAmong the 5 continents below\n1 Africa\n2 Antarctica\n3 Australia | Oceania\n4 Asia\n5 Europe\nArrange the continents from smallest to biggest in terms of its population based on the\nestimated 2004 data\na. 5 3 1 2 4\nb. 1 3 4 2 5\nc. 3 1 4 5 2\nd. 2 4 5 1 3\nThe following statements refer to the African condition that hinders its potential\ntowards economic growth except for one:\na. Diverse natural resources\nb. Insufficient capital technology\nc. Political instability\nd. Small purchasing power\nWhich of the following Asian countries has historical ties with European city and it was\nconsidered as the heart of the Byzantine and Ottoman Empire?\na. Iraq (Mesopotamia)\nb. Israel\nc. Turkey\nd. Russia\nThe following occurrences are all-natural hazards that the world is experiencing across\nthe time except for one:\na. Deforestation\nb. Tsunami\nc. Diastrophism\nd. El Niño and La Niña\nThis is known super continent that broke up million and million years ago.\na. Atlantis\nb. Pangaea\nc. Gondwanaland\nd. Laurasia\nAmong the developing Asian nations, it is widely promoted to be one of the better\nsolutions to poverty and unemployment problems\na. Cooperation\nb. Privatization\nc. Importation\nd. Industrialization\n\n3 | LET REVIEWER UNIVERSITY",
