    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE (6).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nGet more Free LET Reviewers @ www.teachpinas.com\n\nSocial Science Part 6\n1. Without becoming actively involved in\nsocial reform what can sociologists do to\nadvance social activism in their\nprofession?\n\n4. An anthropologist understands other\ncultures from the perspective of an\ninsider?\na. Yes\n\na. Increase social research studies\n\nb. No, should be from the point of view of\nan outsider\n\nb. Improve scientific validity of\nresearches\n\nc. No, should be from the point of view of\nan anthropologist\n\nc. Urge more recent grants\n\nd. Yes, if the insiders are literate.\n\nd. Make their views known public issues\n\n2. Which area of sociology can be\nadvanced so that it is not merely for\nspeculative thinking of theories and\nmethods?\na. Population studies :: on planned\nparenthood\n\n5. When acculturation takes place, what\nhappens?\na. Members of the culture adopt features\nof another\nb. Members of their culture disregard\ntheir culture and adopt another?\n\nb. Applied sociology :: for social change\n\nc. Members of one culture look down on\nother culture.\n\nc. Human studies :: on social ills, e.g. drug\nuse, crime, etc.\n\nd. Members of one culture exclude\nmembers from other cultures.\n\nd. Sociological theory :: for social\nknowledge\n\n3. To select a topic for social research,\npersonal _______ can ensure enthusiasm in\ncompleting a selected study.\na. validity\nb. feasibility\n\n6.When you judge by results regardless of\nyour relations to the people involved,\nwhich Filipino trait do you counteract?\na. Particularism\nb. Supernativalism\nc. Personalism\nd. Non-radionalism\n\nc. interest\nd. relevant\n\n7. if you keep seeing your way of doing\nthings as the right way and everybody\nelse's as the wrong way, you tend to have\nthe attitude called __________.\n\nGet more Free LET Reviewers @ www.teachpinas.com\n\na. cultural relativism\nb. ethnocentrism\nc. cultural pluralism\nd. multiculturalism\n\n8. On what basis is the caste system of\nsocial structure and stratification?\na. Religious beliefs\n\n11. Which illustrate horizontal mobility in\nthe social ladder?\na. The promotion of a teacher to principal.\nb. The demotion from principal to\nteacher.\nc. A teacher remains as a teacher in the\nsame school.\nd. A teacher leaves for the same position\nat another school.\n\nb. Achievement status\nc. Ethnicity\nd. Inherited inequality\n\n12. Karl Marx divided industrial society\ninto bourgeoisie and proletariat.\nWhat was one of his major bases of\nclassification?\n\n9. Which is considered as positive or\nfavorable consequences of tough\ncompetition?\na. Personal stress\nb. Achievement is stimulated\nc. Cooperation is reduced\n\na. Gender role and classification?\nb. Racial and ethnic origins\nc. Whether or not they have royal or noble\nblood\nd. Whether or not they own the means of\nproduction\n\nd. Social inequalities\n\n10. The Chinese minority group in the\nPhilippines adopts the language, history,\nand manners of mainstream Filipino\nculture as its own. What pattern of\ninteraction occurs?\n\n13. Which of the following may result at\nthe departure country when\nFilipino professionals emigrate to other\ncountries?\na. brain drain\n\na. Alteration\n\nb. ethnic diversity\n\nb. Accommodation\n\nc. population increase\n\nc. Amalgamation\n\nd. culture shock\n\nd. Acculturation\n14. If a Catholic researcher makes a study\non polygamy as practiced in\n\nGet more Free LET Reviewers @ www.teachpinas.com\n\nIslam, what influence will likely add\nsubjectivity to his/her findings?\na. Cultural gap\n\n18. When are laws said to be unscientific?\nWhen laws ________.\n\nb. Economic difference\n\na. serve political interests\n\nc. Religious bias\n\nb. are not supported by research\n\nd. Class distinction\n\nc. focus on funding allocation\nd. are irrelevant\n\n15. If government sponsors a research on\nsocial poverty, what factor will\nlikely influence the research?\n\n19. How should social scientist view\nculture?\n\na. Timeliness of study\n\na. Difference in mores of people\n\nb. Lack of funding\n\nb. Refinement in the arts\n\nc. Scope of research\n\nc. All facets of social life\n\nd. Political criticism\n\nd. Ways of ethical conduct\n\n16. What attitude is needed before one\nengages in data-gathering for\n\n20. Color, emblem, gestures, designs,\nwords are part of __________ language that\nmakes man different from animals.\n\nresearch?\na. Return investment for firm\nb. Corporate social responsibility\nc. Press relations for company\nd. Philanthropic dole-out\n\n17. what attitude is needed before one\nengages in data- gathering for research?\na. Prejudgment on result\nb. Bias on hypothesis\nc. Open-minded skepticism\nd. Inadequacy in time\n\na. symbolic\nb. material\nc. denotative\nd. abstract\n\n21. The value marker of ___________ is\nconveyed by the EDSA people power\nrevolution.\na. human rights\nb. justice\nc. freedom\nd. integrity\n\nGet more Free LET Reviewers @ www.teachpinas.com\n\n22. What issue is controversial for church\npeople but is a need of secular society?\na. Birth control\nb. Social media\n\nb. Societies develop from simplicity to\ncomplexity\nc. Social development should not be\ninterfered by legislators\nd. Planned change will disrupt the\nevolution of society.\n\nc. Human rights\nd. Information bill\n\n23. Which can explain the fact that we still\nobserve the nod of respect (mano po) to\nour elders as our forebears?\n\n26. The following facts show Emile\nDurkheim has reason to assume that\nindividuals are products, not creators of\nsociety EXCEPT __________.\na. laws impose conformity\n\na. Punishment for lack of respect\n\nb. man's behavior follows customs\n\nb. Modeling (gaya-gaya)\n\nc. moral codes declare\n\nc. Folkways change slowly\n\nd. systems are made by man\n\nd. Herd mentality\n\n24. What constitutional reform did\nFilipino constitutionalists including those\nwho framed the Malolos Constitution\nintroduce to eliminate the dominance of\nthe church over the state?\na. Expulsion of friars\nb. Taxation on religious schools\n\n27. Which explains Spencer's theory of\nprogressive evolution of human societies?\na. Societies inevitably progress.\nb. Societies have to adapt to survive or\nelse perish\nc. Societies have to complete to survive\nd. Human individuals adapt but not\nhuman societies.\n\nc. Prohibiting religious from political\nmeddling\nd. Separation of church and state\n\n25. What could you accept as true from\nthe varied propositions of Herbert\nSpencer?\na. Societies complete by way of survival of\nthe fittest",
