    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE (6).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\na. The rules are for everybody except to\nthe manager\nb. Apply the rule selectively.\nc. Applies the rule to all.\nd. Change the rule. It is more of an\nexception.\n\nd. conventional practices\n\n84. What do you call the diagrams of\nkinship relations and maps to show how\nthe people are in communities are related\nto one another?\na. Genealogies\nb. Graphics\n\n87. \"He who does not know to look to the\npast will never reach destination.\" To\nwhich Filipino trait does this point?\na. Pakikiisa\nb. Manana Habit\nc. Pakikipagkapwa-tao\nd. Utang na loob\n\nc. Organizers\nd. Spider map\n\n85. To prevent ethnocentrism,\nanthropologists and sociologists advocate\ncross-cultural understanding through a\nconcept known as __________ .\na. cultural relativism\n\n88. Which Filipino trait is laziness\ndisguised in religious grab?\na. Utang na loob\nb. Manana Habit\nc. Bahala na\nd. Pakikisama\n\nb. ethnical relativism\nc. global solidarity\nd. acculturation\n\n86. One reason why we do not progress as\na nation is due to management by\nexception syndrome. What does\nmanagement by exception syndrome\nmean?\n\n89. One of the Filipino's favorite word is\n\"kasi\" (because). This word implies\n__________.\nI. making a scapegoat out of someone or\nsomething\nII. evading responsibility\nIII. posting of action\na. I-II\nb. I-III\n\nGet more Free LET Reviewers @ www.teachpinas.com\n\nc. II-III\nd. I\n\n90. According to one another, we Filipinos\ndo not learn because our messages create\nwhat psychologist call cognitive\ndissonance. Which behavior\ndemonstrates cognitive dissonance?\n\nd. animosity between mainland and Sulu\narchipelago Muslims\n\n93. Among prospects in the Cordillera\nRegion, which is a proven economic\nprospect?\na. Metro Baguio and Easter Cordillera\nGrowth Corridor\n\na. Our Political leaders spend most of\ntheir time arguing.\n\nb. Tourism in Baguio City as summer\ncapital of the country\n\nb. Parents act as role models for their\nchildren.\n\nc. Rice Terraces UNESCO Rice Terraces\nWorld Heritage Site\n\nc. Teacher tells students to some on time\nbut comes late.\n\nd. Metallic and non-metallic mineral\nresources\n\nd. There is so much division in the\ncountry.\n\n91. Among 17 regional subdivisions of the\nPhilippines, which is unique in having its\nown governor and legislative assembly?\na. ARMM\n\n94.What is the highest mountain in\nLuzon?\na. Mt. Buhi :: Sorsogon\nb. Mt. Mayon :: Albay\nc. Mt. Pinatubo ::Zambales\nd. Mt. Pulag :: Benguet\n\nb. Calabarzon\nc.NCR\nd. Davao Region\n\n95. Not among the World Heritage Sites in\nthe Ilocos region is ________ :\na. Santa Maria Church\n\n92. These are reasons why our Muslim\nbrothers in the Southern Philippines\ndeserve autonomy EXCEPT for their\n________.\n\nb. Paoay Church\nc. Vigan\nd. Hunderd Islands Nation Park\n\na. own cultural identify\nb. traditional Muslim homeland\nc. repelling Hispanic and American\ncolonial incursions\n\n96. With its agro-industrial business the\nprovince of ______ has the biggest\n\nGet more Free LET Reviewers @ www.teachpinas.com\n\ncontribution to the economic\ndevelopment in the Ilocos region.\na. Pangasinan\nb. Ilocos Norte\nc. Ilocos Sur\nd. La Union\n\n97. The Presidents of the Republic hailed\nfrom Ilocano provinces EXCEPT _________.\n\n100. The behavioral cause of the\ndiminishing agriculture economy in the\nCalabarzon region is the __________.\na. growth of manufacturing and light-tech\nindustries\nb. urbanization in lifestyle and occupation\nc. focus on tourism promotion of\nhistorical sites\nd. pollution unfavorable to crops\n\na. Ferdinand Marcos\nb. Elpidio Quirino\nc. Gloria Macapagal Arroyo\nd. Fidel B. Ramos\n\n101. Why are lush forest of the mountain\nranges of Aklan, Antique and Capiz\ndescribed as \"accessibility impaired?\"\na. No travelers can pollute them.\n\n98. Which province in Central Luzon can\ncontinue to advance the claim that the\nregion is the Rice Granary of the\nPhilippines?\n\nb. Environment is green.\nc. Cutters and poachers can't reach them.\nd. Good for adventure sports.\n\na. Bataan\n\nc. Tarlac\n\n102. What is the long-term initiative that\nplaced Western Visayas out of the\n\"hotspot areas\" for illegal logging?\n\nd. Zambales\n\na. Surveillance and Monitoring\n\nb. Nueva Ecija\n\nb. Confiscation of illegally cut trees.\n99. Which is NOT a right relationship\nbetween national figures and their\nprovince base in Calabarzon region is\n_________ :\n\nc. Prohibition of possession of forest\nproducts\nd. Reforestation\n\na. Emilio Aguinaldo : Cavate\n\nc. Manuel Quezon :: Quezon City\n\n103. Among advocacy materials posted in\npublic places, which directly relate to\nhealth awareness?\n\nd. Macario Sakay :: Mountain of Rizal\n\na. No smoking\n\nb. Jose Rizal :: Laguna\n\nGet more Free LET Reviewers @ www.teachpinas.com\n\nb. Barya lang po sa umaga\n\nb. kuratsa\n\nc. Priority Seats for Pregnant Women\n\nc. tinikling\n\nd. PWD and Senior Citizen signs\n\nd. pandang\n\n104. The ___________ reverly experience\nmakes the Anti-Atihan pre-Lenten festival\npopular even for foreign tourists.\n\n108. From East Visayas Region, which is\nNOT the right relationship in cultural\nknowledge?\n\na. Black Nazarene\n\na. Kuratsa :: waray dance\n\nb. Lenten\n\nb. Dandansoy :: balad\n\nc. Mardi-gras\n\nc. Tinikling :: bamboo pole\n\nd. Marian\n\nd. Irog nga Tuna :: partriotic song\n\n105. East Visayas Region VII is recognized\nas one of the ________ exporting regions in\nthe country.\n\n109. These are reasons why Negros\nOccidental and Negros Oriental were\nmade into one integrated region EXCEPT\n_________:\n\na. handicraft\nb. fish\nc. coal\nd. sinamay\n\na. one dialect\nb. holistic development\nc. tourism promotion\nd. peace and order management\n\n106. Among landmarks with historical\nsignificance in East Visayas is __________.\na. Santo Nino Shrine\nb. Agas-Agas bridge\nc. Lake Danao\nd. MacArthur Landing Memorial\n\n107. Originating in East Visayas region is\nthe national dance ______ .\na. Itik-Itik\n\n110. These are the cultural relationships\nin the Negros Region EXCEPT ________ :\na. Bacolod City :: Maskara festival\nb. Cadiz City :: sugar central\nc. Baiz City :: what and dolphin watching\nd. Silay City :: ancestral houses\n\n111. The most active volcano in Negros\nRegion is _________ :\na. Hibok-hibok\n\nGet more Free LET Reviewers @ www.teachpinas.com\n\nb. Mayon\nc. Kanlaon\nd. Apo\n112. Desiring to be third force in the\nbalance of water between U.S. and Russia,\nconferences in Bandung (1955), Belgrade\n(1961) and Cario (1964) advanced policy\npositions for security and peace, EXCEPT\n___________.",
