    "body": "Source: 03. CURRENT EVENTS 2019-2020.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n31. On January 21, 2019, a plebiscite takes place with the majority of voters deciding to\nratify the _____________ paving way to the creation of the Bangsamoro Autonomous\nRegion and abolition of the Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao.\nA. Bangsamoro Independence Law\nB. Bangsamoro Republic Law\nC. Bangsamoro Autonomy Law\nD. Bangsamoro Organic Law\n\n32. Which country has developed \"i-Feel you\", an intelligent bracelet which will help\nusers respect social distancing rules?\nA. Germany\nB. France\nC. Italy\nD. Ukraine\n\n33. Who is the US Secretary of State who condemned the exclusion of Taiwan from the\nWorld Health Assembly (WHA)?\nA. Michael Pompeo\nB. Thomas Jefferson\nC. Gina Haspel\nD. Ron Estes\n\n34. The world's highest railway bridge will connect rest of the India with which city?\n\nA. Ladakh\nB. Kashmir\nC. Chail\nD. Munnar\n\n35. On January 27, 2019, at least 20 people were killed while 111 people were injured as\nexplosions rocked the Cathedral of Our Lady of Mount Carmel in _________.\nA. Patikul, Sulu\nB. Davao City\nC. Lamitan, Basilan\nD. Jolo, Sulu\n\n36. What volcano that spewed hazardous eruption last 13th of January, 2020 where all\nresidents near the volcano were advised to evacuate for safety purposes?\nA. Mayon Volcano\nB. Canlaon Volcano\nC. Taal Volcano\nD. Mount Pinatubo\n\n37. What is the hottest temperature recorded in Antarctica as per World Meteorological\nOrganization last February, 2020?\nA. 69.4 °F\nB. 58.7 °F\nC. 75.2 °F\nD. 81.3 °F\n\n38. Which country recently launched a driver-less bullet train capable to ply with a\nspeed up to 350 kilometers per hour and also features 5G connectivity?\nA. USA\nB. Russia\nC. Japan\nD. China\n\n39. The current Speaker the House of the 18th Congress\nA. Allan Peter Cayetano\nB. Gloria Macapagal Arroyo\nC. Sonny Belmonte\nD. Martin Romualdez\n\n40. The current Senate President of the 18th Congress.\nA. Alan Peter Cayetano\nB. Franklin Drilon\nC. Vicente Sotto\nD. Aquilino Pimentel\n\n41. The Philippine Navy Ship that made history by completing the country's first-ever port\ncall in Russia.\nA. BRP Tarlac\nB. BRP Gregorio del Pilar\nC. BRP Ramon Alcaraz\nD. BRP Davao del Sur\n\n42. He is the Philippine President who implemented the Nationwide Smoking Ban.\nA. Benigno Aquino Ill\nB. Fidel Ramos\nC. Rodrigo Duterte\nD. Joseph Estrada\n\n43. On April 30, 2019, he was arrested by the NBI for sharing \"Bikoy\" videos accusing\nPresident Rodrigo Duterte and his family of their involvement in the illegal drug trade.\nA. Maria Ressa\nB. Peter Joemel Advincula\nC. Rodel Jayme\nD. Senator Antonio Trillanes\n\n44. The PH-US Visiting Forces Agreement is a bilateral visiting forces agreement between\nthe Philippines and the United States. On what date did President Duterte announced\nthat he is ending the pact between the two countries?\nA. February 11, 2020\nB. January 25, 2020\nC. February 15, 2020\nD. February 25, 2020\n\n45. Which city has been named World Book Capital for 2020?\nA. Kuala Lumpur\nB. Hanoi\nC. Singapore City\nD. Taipei\n\n46. On October II, 2019, Ethiopian Prime Minister ________________ was awarded the\nNobel\nPeace Prize for helping his country end their 20-year war with Eritrea.\nA. Andrew Holness\nB. Uhuru Kenyatta\nC. Mokgweetsi Masisi\nD. Abiy Ahmed\n\n47. On October 18, 2019, two NASA astronauts Christina Koch and __________________\nmade history by completing the first all-woman spacewalk. They spent 7 hours outside\nthe International Space Station to fix a power issue.\nA. Jessica Meir\nB. Anne McClain\nC. Sally Ride\nD. Peggy Whitson\n\n48. Who was the President of Bolivia who resigned on November 11, 2019 after his 14year reign? Massive protesters accused him of election fraud.\nA. Hugo Banzer\nB. Carlos Mesa\nC. Eduardo Rodriguez\nD. Evo Morales\n\n49. In what Asian country passed a controversial bill that gives citizenship to immigrants\nfrom its three neighboring countries, but not if they are Muslim?\nA. Indonesia\nB. Taiwan\n\nC. Singapore\nD. India\n\n50. Which of the following countries successfully launched its most powerful rocket\n\"Long March-5B\" on its maiden voyage into orbit last 5th of May, 2020?\nA. China\nB. Brazil\nC. Russia\nD. South Africa\n\n51. Who was the world's youngest prime minister elected on December 9, 2019 in\nFinland?\nA. Sanna Marin\nB. Antti Rinne\nC. Juha Sipila\nD. Alexander Stubb\n\n52. Which delegation won the overall ranking in the 30th Southeast Asian Games 2019\nhaving a medal tally of 149 gold, 117 silver, and 121 bronze?\nA. Vietnam\nB. Thailand\nC. Indonesia\nD. Philippines\n\n53. Which country hosted the 34th ASEAN Summit last June 20-23, 2019?\nA. Vietnam\nB. Singapore\n\nC. Thailand\nD. Philippines\n\n54. The following are the new sports coming to the 2020 Summer Olympics EXCEPT\nA. Water polo\nB. Skateboarding\nC. Sport Climbing\nD. Surfing\n\n55. Who was the winning physicist who died last April 1, 2020 and expanded the world's\nunderstanding of magnetism, superconductivity and the structure of matter?\nA. Paul Dirac\nB. Enrico Fermi\nC. Philip Warren Andersen\nD. Hans Bethe\n\n56. The fifth state of matter has been observed by the scientists for the first time in\nspace. What is the name of fifth state of matter?\nA. Bose-Einstein condensates\nB. Bose-Newton condensates\nC. Bose-Curie condensates\nD. Bose-Darwin condensates\n\n57. According to Article 31 of the ASEAN Charter, the Chairmanship of ASEAN shall\nrotate annually, based on the alphabetical order of the English names of Member\nStates. After Singapore chaired and hosted the ASEAN summit last 2018, what country\nwill assume the Chairmanship this 2019?\n\nA. Taiwan\nB. Thailand\nC. Tonga\nD. Tajikistan\n\n58. Who is the first and youngest tribal woman in the world to climb six tallest mountain\npeaks across six continents?\nA. Malavath Poorna\nB. Anuja Vaidya\nC. Shivangi Pathak\nD. Aditi Vaidya\n\n59. What is the name of China's first Mars exploration mission as it celebrated Space\nDay last 24th of April, 2020?\nA. Tianwen-l\nB. Cianwen-l\nC. Rianwen-l\nD. Bianwen-l\n\n60. What are the 24-hour nationwide emergency hotlines?\nA. 999 and 911\nB. 8888 and 911\nC. 8888 and 117\nD. 2363 and 911\n\n61. This volcano erupted on January 12, 2020, 43 years after its previous eruption in 1977.\nIt has reached Alert Level 4 resulted to mass evacuation of residents in different parts of\nthe province.\nA. Mayon Volcano\nB. Taal Volcano\nC. Mount Pinatubo\nD. Mount Kanlaon\n\n62. Where will 2020 Summer Olympics be held?\nA. Argentina\nB. New Zealand\nC. Japan\nD. UAE",
