    "body": "Source: 06. LARGEST AND SMALLEST.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nLARGEST and SMALLEST\n1. Largest continent - Asia\n2. Largest ocean - Pacific\n3. Largest river - Amazon\n4. Largest river basin - Amazon\n5. Largest lake (salt water) - Caspian sea\n6. Largest lake (fresh water) - Lake Superior\n(North America)\n7. Largest artificial lake - Lake Mead at Hoover\nDam, (USA). Originally known as Boulder.\n8. Largest bay - Hudson Bay (North Canada)\n9. Largest gulf - Gulf of Mexico\n10. Largest gorge - Grand Canyon (USA)\n11. Largest sea - South China sea\n12. Largest delta - Sundarbans (India &\nBangladesh)\n13. Largest peninsula - Arabia\n14. Largest island - Greenland\n15. Largest country (in area) - Russia\n17. Largest temple - Angkorwat (Cambodia)\n18. Largest archipelago - Indonesia\n19. Largest airport - King Khalid International\nAirport at Riyadh (Saudi Arabia)\n20. Largest church - St.Peter's Basilica, (Rome)\n21. Largest mosque - Sha Faisal Mosque\n(Islamabad)\n22. Largest embassy - Russian Embassy (Beijing)\n23. Largest war plane - Mirage (France)\n24. Largest prison - Kharkov (Russia)\n25. Largest hotel - MGM Grand Hotel and Casino,\nLas Vegas (USA)\n26. Largest desert - Sahara (Africa)\n27. Largest forest - Coniferous Forests of\nNorthern Russia\n28. Largest stadium - Strahove(Czech Republic)\n\n29. Largest library - United States Library of\nCongress\n30. Largest museum - American Museum of\nNatural History (New York)\n31. Largest animal - Blue whale\n32. Largest land animal - The African Bush\nElephant\n33. Largest democracy - India\n34. Largest electorate - India\n35. Largest town - Mt. Isa (Queensland)\n36. Largest palace - Imperial Palace, Beijing\n37. Largest dam - Three Gorges (China)\n38. Largest landmass - The Eurasian Landmass\n39. Largest park - Wood Buffalo National Park\n(Canada)\n40. Largest zoo - Krugal National Park (South\nAfrica)\n41. Largest river island - Majuli (Assam)\n42. Largest inland sea - Mediterranean sea\n43. Largest canal - Keil Canal in Germany\n44. Largest reef - Great Barrier Reef, (Australia)\n45. Largest city (population) - Tokyo (Japan)\n46. Largest estuary - Ob (Russia)\n47. Largest cave - Mammoth Cave, Kentucky\n(USA)\n48. Largest strait - Tartar strait\n49. Largest wall - The Great Wall (China)\n50. Largest cemetery - Leningrad (Russia)\n51. Largest railway station - Grand Central\nTerminal (New York)\n52. Largest university building - University of\nRiyadh (Saudi Arabia)\n53. Largest open university - Indira Gandhi\nNational Open University (New Delhi)\n\n54. Largest steel plant - Nippon Steel plant\n(Japan)\n55. Largest wingspan - Albatross\n56. Largest active volcano - Mauna lao on Hawaii\n57. Largest planet - Jupiter\n58. Largest bird - Ostrich\n59. Largest sea bird - Albatross\n60. Largest diamond - The Cullinan\n61. Largest parliament - The National People's\nCongress of the People's Republic of China\n62. Largest cold desert - Gobi (Mongolia)\n63. Largest plateau - Pamir (Tibet)\n64. Largest mountain range - The Himalaya\n65. Largest statue - Statue of liberty\n66. Largest bank - World bank (Washington)\n67. Largest army - China\n68. Largest cricket stadium - Melbourne\n(Australia)\n69. Largest navy - USA\n70. Largest airforce - USA\n71. Largest natural satellite - Ganymede (Jupiter)\n72. Largest port - New Jersey\n73. Largest book publishing company - Mc Graw\nHill (New York)\n74. Largest Dome in the World - Astrodome, in\nHousten (U.S.A)\n75. Largest Epic - Mahabharata\n76. Largest carnivorous mammal - Polar Bear\n\n1. Smallest continent - Australia\n2. Smallest ocean - Arctic\n3. Smallest republic - Nauru\n4. Smallest colony - Gibraltar\n5. Smallest state - Vatican\n6. Smallest landmass - The Australian Mainland\n7. Smallest bird - Humming bird\n8. Smallest flowering plant - Wolfia\n9. Smallest planet - Mercury\n10. World's Smallest Museum - Arizona, US",
