    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: LECTURE NOTES SOC SCI (GEN INFO) (Part 1)",
    "body": "Source: 07. LECTURE NOTES - SOC SCI (GEN INFO).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nMark 5:36\n\"Do not be afraid, just\nbelieve.”\n\nGeneral Information\nTHE PHILIPPINE CONSTITUTION\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn case of death, permanent disability, removal from\noffice or resignation of both the President and Vice\nPresident, the next in rank who shall as the\nPresident until the successors shall have been\nelected and qualified is the Senate President.\n(1) Speedy disposition of cases, (2) Have access to\nofficial records and documents, (3) For unions or\nassociations for purposes not contrary to law and (4)\nAssemble and petition the government for redress of\ngrievances are some rights guaranteed to an\nindividual by the constitution.\nThe Presiding Justice of the Sandiganbayan may not\nbe removed from office through impeachment.\nThe following may be removed from office through\nimpeachment: Chief Justice of the Supreme Court,\nMembers of the Supreme Court, Chairman of the\nCommission on Elections and the Chairman of the\nCommission on Audit.\nThe principle of human rights which explains that\nrights of every Filipino cannot be taken away,\nmortgage or surrendered is called Inalienable.\nThe right to just and favorable working conditions\nguarantees every Filipino worker a right to fair\nremuneration for equal work.\nThe liberty of abode and of changing the same may\nbe impaired only upon order of the court.\nWatersheds may be protected through planting\ntrees.\nIn terms of industry classification, the timber\nharvesting is not considered major air pollution in\nsub-sector industry.\nAll kidnap for ransom crimes or other terrorist\nactivities primarily show total disregard for ethnic\nidentity.\nThe minimum age requirement for the members of\nthe House of Representatives to run for an election\nis 25 years old.\nPursuant to RA 6713, temporary and contractual\nworkers may be exempted from filing the annual\nassets and liabilities executed under oath.\nThe right of a person under investigation for\nallegedly committing a criminal act involves right to\nfair trial, right to be presumed innocent, and right to\ncounsel.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nA divestment is supposed to be made thirty (30)\ndays from assumption to office by public official or\nemployee in case a conflict of interest arises.\nSustainable development’s framework is founded on\neconomic, social and environmental dimensions and\ndevelopment. Its essence is the harmonious\nintegration of a sound and viable economy and\nresponsible governance. It is meeting the needs of\nthe present generation without compromising the\nability of future generations to meet their own\nneeds. It is essentially concerned with social\nharmony and the ecological integrity to ensure that\ndevelopment is a life-enhancing process.\nGovernment officials and employees are prohibited\nfrom engaging in partisan political activities except\nin expressing their views on current political\nproblems or issues.\nThe Commission of Human Rights has all the\nfollowing powers and functions: (1) Investigate all\nforms of human rights violations, (2) Exercise\nvisitorial powers over jails and prisons, (3)\nRecommend measures to promote human rights and\n(4) Adopt and implement its operational guidelines\nand rules on procedures.\nConsidering that values are internalized ideas and\nfeelings shared by the members of a society or an\norganization that bind the members together to live\nor establish an orderly life, they are best expressed\nthrough one’s actions.\nThe Commission of Appointments has the authority\nto recommend to the President nominees for the\nmembers of the Supreme Court and judges of the\nlower courts.\nThe authority to call for a constitutional convention\nfor the purpose of proposing amendments thereto,\nor revision thereof, resides in the Congress.\nThe Constitution protects the lives of its unborn\ncitizens. This means that the unborn is given equal\nrights as any born citizen in the country.\nUnder the 1987 Constitution, the State is mandated\nto assign the highest budgetary priority to\nEducation.\nThe President of the Philippines exercises general\nsupervision over all local governments.\nThrough the party list system, the religious sector is\nnot representing in the House of Representatives.\n\nDR. CARL E. BALITA REVIEW CENTER TEL. NO. 735-4098/7350740\n\n-1-\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
    "material_type": "notes",
    "is_premium": false
