    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: LECTURE NOTES SOC SCI (GEN INFO) (Part 3)",
    "body": "Source: 07. LECTURE NOTES - SOC SCI (GEN INFO).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nThe judge is responsible for determining the\nexistence of probable cause for the issuance of a\nwarrant of arrest or search warrant.\nThe right that guarantees similar treatment to all\npersons similarly situated and precludes arbitrary or\nunjust discrimination to secure and safeguard such\nright is called right to equal protection of the law.\nThe managers of government corporations are not\nsubjected to disciplinary authority of the\nOmbudsman.\nThe Commission of Elections exercises original and\nexclusive jurisdiction over all contests relating to the\nelection returns and the qualifications of the\nPresident and Vice president.\nDecentralization is the process of transferring the\nbasic powers from national to local governments to\nallow maximum participation of the citizens in\ngovernmental and community activities.\nAll persons, shall before conviction, be bailable by\nsufficient sureties, or be released on recognizances\nas may be provided by law except when charged\nwith offenses punishable by reclusion perpetua\naccompanied by a strong evidence of guilt.\nThe intention of the law in presuming the innocence\nof an accused in a criminal prosecution is to prevent\nthe conviction of an innocent person.\nThe Constitution provides that the Philippines\nrenounces war as an instrument of national policy,\nthis means that the Philippines will not engage in\naggressive war.\nAn effective and speedy remedy on the part of the\npeople to remove an elective official who is not\nperforming his/her functions to their satisfaction is\nthrough initiative.\nIn a barangay election, losing candidates are eligible\nfor appointment or re-employment to any office in\nthe government.\nThe statement, “A law which hears before it\ncondemns, which proceeds upon inquiry, and\nrenders judgment only after trial” best describes the\nessence of due process of law.\nSexual harassment may not be a ground for\nimpeachment.\nMilitary power can be delegated by the President.\nThe court has resisted the clamor to issue a\ntemporary injunction for the sake of expediency.\nThe Department of Interior and Local Government\n(DILG) can declare that a city is a highly urbanized\ncity.\n\nR.A.\n6713:\nCONDUCT\nAND\nETHICAL\nSTANDARDS FOR PUBLIC OFFICIALS AND\nEMPLOYEES\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe following are the terms of conduct for\ngovernment employees: (1) Political neutrality, (2)\nProfessionalism, (3) Nationalism and patriotism, (4)\nJustness and sincerity.\nThe following exemplify commitment to public\nservice: (1) Exposing graft and corruption, (2)\nReporting hazards to health in the community, (3)\nPreserving public property and domain, (4) Using\noffice supplies economically.\nTechnical positions allow appointments of relatives\nby consanguinity or affinity by the appointing\nauthority.\nFrom the time of separation from the government\nservice, public officials are prohibited from accepting\nemployment in any private enterprise previously\nregulated by their office for a period of one year.\nEntrepreneurial activities of government employees\nmay be allowed subject to all of the following\nconditions: (1) These are not done during office\nhours, (2) These are not done within the required\n40-hour-a-week period, (3) These do not require\nsources and facilities, (4) The income form\nentrepreneurial activities does not exceed half of the\nemployees’ annual income.\nThe obligation of government officials and\nemployees to be at all times answerable for their\nmisconduct to the people from whom the\ngovernment derives its power is known as public\naccountability.\nWithin the prescribed period of time public officials\nand employees are required to file their statement of\nassets and liabilities and financial disclosure in the\nfollowing instances: (1) Assumption of office, (2)\nCompulsory retirement, (3) Voluntary resignation,\n(4) Acceptance of foreign scholarship.\nFree voluntary service refers to services rendered by\ncivil servants without compensation.\nSimple living is a norm of conduct described by the\nstatement “Public officials and employees and their\nfamilies shall lead modest lives appropriate for their\npositions and income.”\nEvery government agency is required to develop,\nupdate regularly, and make available to the\ntransacting public the performance targets\nPolitical neutrality means that public officials and\nemployees shall provide service to anyone without\nunfair discrimination and regardless of party\naffiliation of preference.\nCommitment to public interest may be exemplified\nwhen officials and employees always uphold public\ninterest over personal interest.\nThe following are considered as primary functions of\nthe Civil Service Commission: (1) Institutionalize a\nmanagement\nclimate\nconductive\nto\npublic\naccountability, (2) Establish a career service and\nadopt measures to promote morale, efficiency,\nintegrity, responsiveness, progressiveness and\ncourtesy in the civil service, (3) Strengthen the merit\n\nRA 6173 or “Code of Conduct and Ethical Standards\nfor public Officials and Employees” covers the\nfollowing: (1) Temporary employees; (2) Non-career\nemployees; (3) Elective and appointive officials; (4)\nMilitary and police personnel.\nDR. CARL E. BALITA REVIEW CENTER TEL. NO. 735-4098/7350740\n\n-3-",
