    "body": "Source: 07. LECTURE NOTES - SOC SCI (GEN INFO).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nand rewards system, (4) Integrate all human\nresources development programs for all levels and\nranks.\nPublic officials or employees are required to identify\nand disclose under oath their relatives in the\ngovernment who are within fourth civil degree of\nrelationship.\nHeads\nof government-owned\nor\ncontrolled\ncorporations (GOCC) are required to submit their\nStatement of Assets Liabilities and Net Worth to the\nOffice of the Government Corporate Counsel.\nChairpersons and Commissioners and Constitutional\nCommissions file their statement of Assets and\nLiabilities and Net Worth with their respective\noffices.\nThe following are qualifications to evaluate the most\noutstanding government employee: (1) The level of\nsalary, (2) The length of service and consistency of\nperformance, (3) The obscurity of the position, (4)\nThe unique and exemplary quality of a certain\nachievement.\nThe Office of the Ombudsman is mandated to\ndetermine the causes of inefficiency, red tape,\nmismanagement, fraud and corruption in the\ngovernment.\nProfessionals are best described as performing and\ndischarging one’s duties with the highest degree of\nexcellence, intelligence and skills.\nConflict of interest occurs when a public official or\nemployee in an officer of a business establishment\nthe interest of which affects the faithful performance\nof his/her official duty.\n\n\n\nPEACE AND HUMAN RIGHTS CONCEPTS AND\nVALUES\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Commission on Rights has all of the following\npowers and functions: (1) Investigate all forms of\nhuman rights violation, (2) Exercise visitorial powers\nover jails and prisons, (3) Recommend measures to\npromote human rights, (4) Adopt and implement its\noperational guidelines and rules on procedures.\nOn December 10, 1948, the UN General Assembly\nadopted the Universal Declaration of Human Rights\nwith the purpose of releasing of prisoners of war\n(POW) ill held in different concentration camps\naround the world.\nThe following are functions or services that\nvolunteers in the government can perform:\ninvestigation, advisory, counseling, humanitarian.\nValues development programs include all of the\nfollowing: (1) Philippine history, culture and\ntradition, (2) Nationalism and patriotism, (3) Ethical\nand moral values, (4) Democracy in a free and just\nsociety.\nThe basic criterion of a true value is that it is freely\nchosen among alternatives being fully aware of its\nconsequences.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe primary objective for the nationwide\nimplementation of the Values Integration for\nGovernment Renewal (VIGOR) Program is to enrich\nFilipino work and moral values.\nPeace is what people yearn and hope for they can\nsettle on their respective homes without fear and\ntherefore focus on improving their quality of life.\nJaywalking, throwing garbage anywhere, vandalism,\nnot waiting in line and tardiness are manifestations\nof lack of discipline.\nIn being economical, one must decide where the\nbest place to begin really in some families engages\nin\npetty\neconomic\nthat\nrequires\neffort\ndisproportionate to the money saved.\n\nENVIRONMENTAL ISSUES\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProtecting coastal ecosystems is the best way to\nensure sustainable fish supply.\nIncineration is the proper way of disposing medical\nand hospital wastes.\nThe main purpose of waste segregation is to turn\nwaste into resource.\nPollution of air is the most damaging effect that a\ncement industry can do on the environment.\nThe most important aspect with regard to population\nas a factor in environmental quality is the equitable\naccess to resources.\nLogging is the most destructive cause of forest\ndegradation.\nThe dominant source of air pollution in the\nMetropolitan area is motor vehicles.\nRe-using is the most environment-friendly treatment\nfor a used glass bottle.\nAn environment impact assessment ensures that the\nnegative impact is mitigated.\nThe ozone layer is vital in the preservation of life on\nearth because it protects us from the harmful effect\nof ultraviolet rays.\nIndigenous people can best protect the forests in\nthe long run.\nForests serve as habitat to wildlife.\nPutting some dams along rivers can negatively affect\nmarine fishes because some marine fishes spend\npart of their life cycle upstream.\nPlanting variety of crops on a place of land is more\nadvisable than planting only one kind of crop\nbecause vulnerability to plant pests is less.\nWatersheds are important in the nation’s survival\nbecause they sustain water supply.\nBiogas is a renewable source of energy.\nSorting of garbage is necessary to enable recycling\nor reuse.\nMonoculture cropping or planting a single crop in a\nlarge area is not advisable because it promotes pest\ninfestation.\nCoral reefs are of great importance because they\nserve as haven for young growing fish and small\naquatic animals.\n\nDR. CARL E. BALITA REVIEW CENTER TEL. NO. 735-4098/7350740\n\n-4-\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe biggest threat to biodiversity, which is the\nvariety and variability among living things, is the\ndestruction of wildlife habitats.\nAn area that has been logged will have greater\nerosion if the area is cultivated for cash crops.\nA rainforest is a forest in tropics.\nFishery resources in marine and coastal waters may\nbe considered as “open access resources” because\nof the difficulty in marking sea boundaries.\nThe lasting environmental impact of a large-scale\nmining operation comes from mine tailings.\nChlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) are popular as\npropellants and insulting agents because they are\nreactive.\nThrowing paper into the rivers is objectionable\nbecause it is unpleasant to see floating papers in the\nriver.\nDynamite fishing is the major cause of coral reef\ndestruction.\nExcessive build-up of carbon dioxide causes both\nglobal warming and ozone depletion.\nLead is a heavy metal is emitted by gasoline-fueled\nvehicles and is potentially poisonous substances that\nare particularly harmful to children. According to the\nWorld Health Organization (WHO), inhalation of this\nsubstance can severely affect a child’s behavior and\ndecrease intelligent quotient among children with\nhigh levels of concentration in the blood and bone\nmarrow.\nThe most dangerous effect of deforestation is soil\nerosion.\nSolid waste Management Program is the pollution\nmanagement program implemented by the DENR\nwhich includes disclosure of industries polluting the\nenvironment.\nFarmers migrate to the uplands primarily because of\nthe greater amount of resources in the forest.\n\nDR. CARL E. BALITA REVIEW CENTER TEL. NO. 735-4098/7350740\n\n-5-",
