    "body": "Source: 20. SOCIAL SCIENCE REVIEWER N.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n32. This school of thought views the self as socially constructed in relation to social forces\nand structures and the product of ongoing negotiations of meanings.\na. Functionalism\nb. Structuralism\nc. Symbolic Interactionism\nd. Idealism\n33. These are rules and expectations by which a society guides the behavior of its members.\na. Norms\nb. Language\nc. Culture\nd. Beliefs\n34. An example of this concept is when a teacher and fellow students give you the message\nthat you are 'smart', you will come to think of yourself as an intelligent person.\na. Reflection\nb. Equilibrium\nc. Looking-glass self\nd. Juhari Window\n35. Which of the following qualities should be developed by the pillar, Learning to Live\nTogether?\na. Strong appreciation of the diversity of the human race\nb. Readiness to take risks and resolve or manage conflicts\nc. Scientific spirit and an inquiring mind\nd. Complete fulfillment of humans, in all the richness of his/her personality\n36. Which dimension of health focuses on a person's desire to learn and gain knowledge?\na. Intellectual\nb. Physical\nc. Social\nd. Spiritual\n37. According to this theory, language and culture influence each other.\na. Linguistic-Relativity Theory\nb. Functionalist Theory\nc. Symbolic Interactionism\nd. Consensus Theories\n38. The following are considered communication barriers except __________.\na. Semantics\nb. Channel\nc. Value Judgements\nd. Mixed Signals\n39. Treating others alike would offend against the notions of appropriateness because\npeople have ________.\na. Different needs and deserts\nb. Different wants and priority\nc. Alike wants and priority\nd. Alike deserts and wants\n40. It is the process of learning some new traits from other culture.\na. Enculturation\nb. Acculturation\nc. Assimilation\nd. Accommodation\n41. Which of the following is not a previous title of Religious Education?\na. Religious Knowledge\nb. Religious Teachings\nc. Religious Instruction\nd. Christian Life Education\n42. Justice in education includes of the following __________.\na. Fair Treatment\nb. Equal Treatment\nc. Appropriate Treatment\nd. Provisions of Special Schools\n43. Select the option that is not an example of the Material dimension.\n4 | LET REVIEWER UNIVERSITY\n\n44.\n\n45.\n\n46.\n\n47.\n\n48.\n\n49.\n\n50.\n\na. Important Landmarks\nb. Holy Places\nc. Yahweh\nd. Special Buildings\nThe following are characteristics of culture except __________.\na. it is learned\nb. it is dynamic\nc. it is diverse\nd. it is absolute\nIt is the term used for a process in which an individual entirely loses any awareness of\nhis/her previous group identity and takes on the culture and attitudes another group.\na. Enculturation\nb. Acculturation\nc. Assimilation\nd. Accommodation\nIt is the most obvious form of paralanguage is body language, also known as _________.\na. Semantics\nb. Pragmatics\nc. Kinesics\nd. Mannerism\nThe belief in a God or supernatural being is best defined as _________.\na. Righteous\nb. Religion\nc. Parable\nd. Dimension\nAccording to Glazer, it is an anthropological approach which posits that all cultures are\nof equal value and need to be studied in a neutral point of view.\na. Cultural Sensitivity\nb. Cultural equilibrium\nc. Cultural Relativism\nd. Cultural Balance\nIt is a general or widespread agreement among all members of a particular society.\na. Conflict\nb. Consensus\nc. Mutualism\nd. Association\nIt is an arrangement in which employees use computers to perform their regular work\nresponsibilities at home or elsewhere.\na. Telecommuting\nb. Telecommunication\nc. Teleconferencing\nd. Television\n\n5 | LET REVIEWER UNIVERSITY",
