    "topic_slug": "social-studies-araling-panlipunan",
    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: THE PHILIPPINE CONSTITUTION PART 1 (Part 1)",
    "body": "Source: 23. THE PHILIPPINE CONSTITUTION PART 1.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nTHE PHILIPPINE CONSTITUTION\nPART I - 30 ITEMS\n1. Which of the following is not mentioned in the declaration of policy of public officials in\nR.A. 6713?\nA. They shall be accountable to the people\nB. They shall uphold the constitution of the republic of the Philippines\nC. They shall lead modest lives\nD. They shall discharge their duties with utmost responsibilities\n2. In art. Iv, section 4, unless by their act or omission they are deemed, under the law, to\nhave renounced it, citizens of the Philippines who marry aliens shall:\nA. Lose their citizenship\nB. Have the choice to select which citizenship to relinquish\nC. Retain their citizenship\nD. Automatically adopt dual citizenship, unless contravened by laws of the country\nof his spouse\n3. What arises when a public official is an officer of a private corporation which affects his\nfaithful performance of official duty?\nA. Conflict of interest\nB. Redundancy\nC. Double remuneration\nD. Double compensation\n4. Public officials and employees shall provide service to everyone without unfair\ndiscrimination and regardless of what?\nA. Length of service\nB. Party affiliation\nC. Public office\nD. Religion\n\n5. In Art. II, Section 21, the state shall promote comprehensive rural development and what\nrelated field?\nA. Countryside improvement\nB. Agrarian reform\nC. Urban planning\nD. Agricultural economy\n6. What body is mentioned as the protector of the people and the state?\nA. Executive Government\nB. Department of National Defense\nC. Armed Forces of The Philippines\nD. Philippine National Police\n7. The state shall promote a just and dynamic social order that will ensure the prosperity\nand independence of the nation and Free the people from what?\nA. Poverty\nB. Law-breaking\nC. Corruption\nD. Injustice\n8. The state values the dignity of every ___________ and guarantees full respect for human\nrights.\nA. living thing\nB. natural-born citizen\nC. human person\nD. religion or belief\n9. “Commodatum” is a type of:\nA. loan\nB. elective office\nC. government agency\n\nD. code\n10. Which of the following is not a power or function of the commission on human rights?\nA. Monitor the Philippine government's compliance with international treaty\nobligations on human rights\nB. Initiate proceedings to inculpate foreigners who trample upon the rights of other\naliens in Philippine territory.\nC. Appoint its officers and employees in accordance with law\nD. Establish a continuing program of research, education, and information to\nenhance respect for the primacy of human rights\n11. Public officials and employees shall not solicit or accept gifts, except when it is:\nA. scholarship to a degree program\nB. of nominal value\nC. in foreign legal tender\nD. medical treatment\n12. What is the maximum amount of time that a public official or employee must respond\nto letters sent by the public?\nA. 15 working days\nB. one month\nC. seven working days\nD. one week\n13. The constitution defines the following as citizens of the philippines except:\nA. those who are citizens of the philippines at the time of the adoption of this\nconstitution or those whose fathers or mothers are citizens of the philippines\nB. those who are naturalized in accordance with law\nC. those who were born outside the national territory of the philippines but whose\nparents were born as filipino citizens\n\nD. those born before january 17, 1973, of filipino mothers, who elect philippine\ncitizenship upon reaching the age of majority\n14. In article ii, the state affirms what aspect! As a primary social economic force as it\nprotects the rights of workers and promote their welfare?\nA. human rights\nB. industry\nC. labor\nD. agriculture\n15. Which of the following will not be appropriate on the blank: public officials and\nemployees shall perform and discharge their duties with the highest degree of\n_____________.\nA. intelligence and skill\nB. attitude\nC. excellence\nD. professionalism\n16. No educational institution shall .be. Established exclusively for aliens and no group of\naliens shall comprise more than _______________ of the enrollment in any school.\nA. one-fifth\nB. one-half\nC. one-third\nD. one-fourth\n17. In article xiv, __________ shall be enjoyed in all institutions of higher learning.\nA. freedom of education\nB. scholarships\nC. academic freedom\nD. liberal arts\n\n18. The state recognizes the vital role of the ______________ in nation building and shall\npromote and protect their physical, moral, spiritual, intellectual and social well-being\nA. youth\nB. family\nC. government\nD. women\n19. The state shall pursue an independent foreign policy. In its relations with other states, the\nparamount consideration shall be each of the following, except:\nA. Territorial Integrity\nB. Nationalized Control\nC. National Interest &The Right To Self-Determination\nD. National Sovereignty\n20. Article ii, section 6 states that separation of ___________ and state shall be inviolable.\nA. President\nB. Church\nC. Politics\nD. Military\n21. “relatives” refer to all persons related to a public official to what degree of\nconsanguinity?\nA. Fourth\nB. Second\nC. Third\nD. First\n22. In Art. XIII, what is the national language of the Philippines?\nA. Filipino\nB. Pilipino\nC. Tagalog\n\nD. English\n23. What authority is supposed to be supreme over the military?\nA. Judicial\nB. Civilian\nC. Presidential\nD. Democratic\n24. According to Art. XIII, the state is supposed to ensure that teaching will attract and retain\nits rightful share of the best available talents through _________ and other means of job\nsatisfaction and fulfillment.\nA. Professional Growth\nB. Adequate Remuneration\nC. Continuous Training\nD. Stagnating Salaries\n25. In section ii of the declaration of principles, the Philippines renounces ______________ as\nan instrument of national policy.\nA. Lawlessness\nB. Com-Communism\nC. Extra-Territoriality\nD. War\n26. The national territory of the republic of the Philippines includes each of the following (in\nthe territorial islands and waters) except:\nA. The Insular Shelves\nB. The Overseas Domains\nC. The Subsoil\nD. The Seabed\n27. Family of public officials or employees include spouses and who else?",
