    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: THE PHILIPPINE CONSTITUTION PART 2 (Part 1)",
    "body": "Source: 24. THE PHILIPPINE CONSTITUTION PART 2.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nTHE PHILIPPINE CONSTITUTION\nPART II - 30 ITEMS\n1. Prohibitions on outside employment does not include someone who:\na. Work for a private enterprise regulated by their office\nb. Recommends any person to a position to a company which has transactions\nwith his/her office\nc. Hires relatives higher than the fifth degree of consanguinity or affinity\nd. Engages in private practice of his/her profession in conflict with official functions\n2. What is the title of Article I of the 1986 constitution?\na. Transitory Provisions\nb. National Territory\nc. Preamble\nd. Bill of Rights\n3. In section 4, what should public officials and employees always uphold over and\nabove personal matters?\na. R.A. 6713\nb. The Philippine Flag\nc. The Public Interest\nd. The Constitution\n4. In section 21, no person shall be ________________ put in jeopardy of punishment for the\nsame offense. If an act is punished by a law and an ordinance, conviction or acquittal\nunder either shall constitute a bar to another prosecution for the same act.\na. innocently\nb. legally\nc. inadequately\nd. twice\n\n5. The committee on awards to outstanding public officials is headed by chairman of the\ncivil service commission and who else?\na. Ombudsman\nb. Dilg Secretary\nc. Sandiganbayan\nd. Solicitor General\n6. The state is supposed to enhance the right of teachers to ______________\na. Organize into unions and associations\nb. Demand a humane amount of salary\nc. Professional advancement\nd. Strike against oppressive superiors\n7. Public officials and employees should defend philippine sovereignty against what?\na. Foreign intrusion\nb. National and international conflicts\nc. Other southeast Asian neighbors\nd. Influence5 of other countries\n8. No involuntary servitude in any from shall exist except:\na. as punishment for a crime whereof the party shall be duly convicted\nb. in times of national emergency\nc. in cases of invasion or rebellion when the public safety requires it\nd. when the writ of habeas corpus is necessitated\n9. Article v states the following as requirements for citizens to exercise suffrage except:\na. Those not otherwise disqualified by law\nb. Those who are at least eighteen years of age\nc. Those who shall have resided in the philippines for at least one year and in the\nplace wherein they propose to vote for at least six months immediately\npreceding the election\n\nd. Those who do not have pending cases involving treason against the state\n10. What do you call the transfer of title or disposal of interest in property in favor of\nsomeone not one’s spouse or relative?\na. endowment\nb. divestment\nc. inheritance\nd. reparation\n11. The state is tasked to protect and strengthen the __________ as a basic autonomous\nsocial institution\na. Society\nb. Filipino Citizen\nc. Barangay\nd. Family\n12. Which of the following should be made accessible to the public within reasonable\nworking hours?\na. Statement of accountability\nb. Public documents\nc. Appointments with public officials\nd. Assets and liabilities\n13. What should head of agencies submit within 45 working days from the end of the\nyear?\na. contract of assets and liabilities\nb. annual performance report\nc. recapitulation account\nd. performance rating of employees\n\n14. In Art. XIV, senators and members of the house of representatives should receive what\nannual salary unless they, give themselves increases?\na. 204,000 pesos\nb. 60 million pesos\nc. 600,000 pesos\nd. 240,000 pesos\n15. What do you call those who are citizens of the Philippines from birth without having to\nperform any act to acquire or perfect their Philippine citizenship?\na. Natural-born citizens\nb. Citizens of the republic of the Philippines\nc. Naturalized citizens\nd. Primary citizens\n16. Which of the following is not mentioned to be essential for the enjoyment by all the\npeople of the blessings of democracy?\na. Protect ton o life, liberty and property\nb. Promotion of the general welfare\nc. Maintenance of peace and order\nd. Preservation of patrimony and loyalty to flag and country\n17. The state recognizes the role of women in nation-building, and shall ensure the\n________________ of women and men.\na. Bill of rights\nb. Inherent freedom\nc. Fundamental equality\nd. Safety and security\n18. In Art. III, section 20, no person shall be imprisoned for ______________\na. Debt or non-payment of a poll tax\nb. Actions stemming from his political beliefs\n\nc. More than 25 years\nd. A capital offense\n19. Who may be required, under conditions provided by law, to render personal military or\ncivil service?\na. Male citizens 18 - 65 years old\nb. All Filipinos 18 - 65 years old\nc. All citizens\nd. Natural born Filipinos\n20. Who are not mentioned as public employees in R.A. 6713?\na. Military personnel\nb. Temporary government employees\nc. Agency personnel in government offices\nd. Police personnel\n21. To foster patriotism and nationalism, accelerate social progress and promote total\nhuman liberation and development, the state shall give priority to each one except:\na. Education\nb. Arts, Culture and Sports\nc. Labor And Livelihood\nd. Science And Technology\n22. In Art XIV, the state shall protect and promote the right of all citizens to _____________\neducation at all levels and shall take appropriate steps to make such education\naccessible to all.\na. Quality\nb. Free\nc. Cheap\nd. Inexpensive\n\n23. What government agency is tasked to adopt positive measures to promote\nobservance of standards and continuing research and experimentation in order to\nraise the level of these standards?\na. Office of the president\nb. Civil service commission\nc. The office of the ombudsman\nd. Department of the interior and local government\n24. The constitution expects the state to provide each of the following with training in\ncivics, vocational efficiency and other skills, except:\na. Ex-convicts\nb. Out-of-school youth\nc. Adult citizens\nd. The disable\n25. The state shall develop a self-reliant and independent national economy effectively\ncontrolled by whom?\na. Filipinos\nb. Natural-born citizens\nc. The government\nd. Their executive branch\n26. According to Art. XIII, the state is supposed to assign the highest budgetary priority to\na. Education\nb. The pork barrel congressmen and senators\nc. The office of the president\nd. Foreign debt servicing\n27. Where is the legislative power vested (except to the extent reserved to the people by\nthe provision on initiative and Referendum)?\na. Congress of the Philippines",
