otabato\n(064) 248-2138\nop@usm.edu.ph\nwww.usm.edu.ph\nREGION XIII - CARAGA REGION\n\nJOY C. CAPISTRANO\nPresident\n\nAGUSAN DEL SUR STATE COLLEGE OF AGRICULTURE\nAND TECHNOLOGY\nBunawan, Agusan del Sur\n(085) 266-2525\nop@asscat.edu.ph\nwww.asscat.edu.ph\n\nANTHONY M. PENASO\nPresident\n\nCARAGA STATE UNIVERSITY\nAmpayon, Butuan City\n(085) 341-7739; 342-1079\nop@carsu.edu.ph\nwww.carsu.edu.ph\n\nGEORGE M. COLORADO\nOfficer-in-Charge\n\nNORTHEASTERN MINDANAO STATE UNIVERSITY\nTandag, Surigao del Sur\n(086) 211-4221\nnemsuop@sdssu.edu.ph\nwww.sdssu.edu.ph\n\n133\n\nGREGORIO Z. GAMBOA JR.\nPresident\n\nSURIGAO DEL NORTE STATE UNIVERSITY\nSurigao City\n(086) 826-6346\nwww.ssct.edu.ph\n\nBANGSAMORO AUTONOMOUS REGION IN MUSLIM MINDANAO\nHANYA M. ADIONG\nOfficer-In-Charge\nCHARISMA S. UTUTALUM\nPresident\nMUTTI A. ASAALI\nPresident\n\n134\n\nADIONG MEMORIAL POLYTECHNIC STATE COLLEGE\nDitsaan-Ramain, Lanao del Sur\nSULU STATE COLLEGE\nJolo, Sulu\nwww.sulustatecollege.edu.ph\nTAWI-TAWI REGIONAL AGRICULTURAL COLLEGE\nBongao, Tawi-Tawi\n\nLEGISLATIVE\nBRANCH\nLEGISLATIVE\nBRANCH\n\nLEGISLATIVE BRANCH\nAs provided for by the Constitution, the Congress of the Philippines is the\nbicameral legislative body of the Philippine Government which has the power\nto enact laws, including the General Appropriations Act. In addition to\nits legislative mandate, the Congress also performs functions such as the\nconfirmation of Presidential appointments,impeachment, declaration of the\nexistence of a state of war and concurrence or confirmation of the amnesty\ngranted by the President.\nThe Congress is divided into two chambers: the Senate and the House of\nRepresentatives.\nThe Senate consists of 24 duly elected Senators, 12 of whom are replaced or\nre-elected every three years, to ensure continuity of policies, as well as the\navailability of experienced members who can help and train newcomers in\nthe discharge of duties.\nThe House of Representatives of the 19th Congress is composed of 251\nGeographical District Representatives and 60 Sectoral Representatives. The\nSectoral Representatives constitute about 24 percent of the total number of\nthe Members of the House. Each Representative serves for a term of three (3)\nyears, and can be re-elected for two (2) additional consecutive terms.\n\nSENATE OF THE PHILIPPINES\n(19th CONGRESS)\nGSIS Building, Financial Center\nRoxas Blvd., 1300 Pasay City\nTrunkline: (632) 8552-6601 to 70\nwww.senate.gov.ph\n\nJUAN MIGUEL F. ZUBIRI\nloc. 6501 to 6505; 8552-6813; 8804-0270 TF\nSenate President\n\nLOREN B. LEGARDA\nloc. 6801, 8617\nSenate President Pro Tempore \nJOEL J. VILLANUEVA\nMajority Floor Leader\nAQUILINO L. PIMENTEL III\nMinority Floor Leader\n\nloc. 4675; 8807-9453; 8552-6781 TF\nloc. 5548 TF\n\nJOSEPH VICTOR G. EJERCITO\nDeputy Majority Floor Leader\n\nloc. 5851\n\nMARK A. VILLAR\nDeputy Majority Floor Leader\n\nloc. 5801 to 5804; 8330-6070",
