gov.ph\n\nPAISALIN P. TAGO\nMinister\n\nMinistry of Transportation and Communication\n(064) 557-3065; 552-0055\nmotc@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nHUSSEIN P. MUÑOZ\nMinister\n\nMinistry of Public Order and Safety\n(064) 425-5514\nmpos@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nEDUARD U. GUERRA\nMinister\n\nMinistry of Public Works\n(064) 557-0881\nmpw@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nRAISSA H. JAJURIE\nMinister\n\nMinistry of Social Services and Development\n(064) 552-3544; 4521-5856\nmssd@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nABU AMRI A. TADDIK\nMinister\n\nMinistry of Trade, Investments and Tourism\n(064) 421-1248; 421-1234; 557-2819; 421-7729 F\nmtit@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\n238\n\nATTACHED OFFICES\nSALEM Y. LINGASA\nChairperon\n\nBangsamoro Commission for the Preservation of Cultural Heritage\n(064) 421-1470; 552-0028\nbch@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nSAID Z. SALENDAB\nExecutive Director\n\nBangsamoro Pilgrimage Authority\nbpa@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nMOHAJIRIN T. ALI\nDirector-General\n\nBangsamoro Planning and Development Authority\n(064) 557-2795; 557-2797\nbpda@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nNU-MAN C. CALUDTIAG\nChairperson\n\nBangsamoro Sports Commission\n(064) 552-1553\nbsc@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nBAINON G. KARON\nChairperson\n\nBangsamoro Women Commission\n(064) 421-2562\nrcbw@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nABUHURAIRA ABDULRAHMAN UDASAN\nBangsamoro Mufti\n\nBangsamoro Darul-Ifta’\n(064) 557-0787\nbdi@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nHISHAM S. NANDO\nExecutive Director\n\nDevelopment Academy of the Bangsamoro\n(064) 552-0173\ndab@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nEDGARDO B. RAMIREZ\nDirector III\n\nOffice for Settler Communities\nosc@bangsamoro.govph\n\nMARJANIE S. MIMBANTAS MACASALONG\nChairperson\n\nBangsamoro Youth Comission\n(064) 557-0347; 552-3168\nbyc@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nAMEEN ANDREW L. ALONTO\nExecutive Director\n\nBureau of Information Office-BARMM\n(064) 552-3032; 521-9427\ninfo@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nJONATHAN M. MANTIKAYAN\nExecutive Director III\n\nBangsamoro Information and Communications Technology Office\n(064) 421-2298\nbicto@bangsamoro.gov.ph\n\nSAMCIA U. EBRAHIM\nDirector II\n\nCooperative and Social Enterprise Authority\ncsea@bangsamoro.gov.ph\nBANGSAMORO TRANSITION AUTHORITY\n(064) 552-0057; 425-5208\nrecords@bta.gov.ph\n\nRABY B. ANGKAL\nPANGALIAN M. BALINDONG\nSHA ELIJAH B. DUMAMA-ALBA\nABDULGANI B. CALUDTIAG\n\nSecretary General\nParliament Speaker\nFloor Leader\nSergeant-at-Arms\n\n239\n\n240\n\nDIPLOMATIC\nOFFICES AND\nINTERNATIONAL\nORGANIZATIONS\n\nDIPLOMATIC OFFICES AND\nINTERNATIONAL ORGANIZATIONS\n\nDIPLOMATIC OFFICES\nThe Philippine government has welcomed 203 diplomatic and consular\nmissions to the country.\nMetro Manila hosts most of these embassies, which conduct a full range of\ndiplomatic activities and services, including the development of commercial,\neconomic, cultural and scientific relations between the Philippines and their\nrespective home countries, and the issuance of passports, travel documents,\nand visas. Some consular missions are located outside of Metro Manila, but\nstill in key cities of the archipelago, primarily to facilitate the delivery of\nservices to their citizens, as well as to Filipinos.\nThere are resident and non-resident missions. The former have embassies\nor chanceries, with the respective head of mission located in the Philippines.\nThe latter, on the other hand, have missions based outside the country.\nThe premier diplomatic mission in the Philippines is that of the Holy See, the\nApostolic Nunciature. Its head, the Apostolic Nuncio, is by tradition the Dean\nof the Diplomatic Corps.\n\nINTERNATIONAL ORGANIZATIONS\nInternational organizations that have established offices in the Philippines\nare focused on various functions and issues, depending on their mandates.\nThese include information and monitoring of global trends, delivery of\nservices such as health, social action and humanitarian aid, providing venues\nfor economic and political discourse, and settling of disputes. While most\nof these organizations have their primary headquarters in Metro Manila,\na number of them have regional offices to provide better access to their\nstakeholders and clients.\n\nDIPLOMATIC AND CONSULAR MISSIONS\n\nCountry\n\nRepresentative\n\nHOLY SEE\nH.E. CHARLES JOHN BROWN III\nApostolic Nunciature\nApostolic Nuncio\n2140 Taft Avenue, Manila \n8521-0306; 8521-0307; 8521-1235 F\nna.philippines@diplomat.va\nANGOLA\nEmbassy of the Republic of Angola\nUnit 2003 One Global Place\n5th Avenue cor. 25th Street\nBonifacio Global City, Taguig City\n8892-4081; 8892-4082; 8892-4195 F\nembangola@pacific.net.ph\nARGENTINA\nEmbassy of the Argentine Republic\n8/F Liberty Center Bldg., 104 H. V. Dela Costa St.\nSalcedo Village, Makati City\n8845-3218; 8845-3219; 8845-3238; 8845-3220 F\nefili@mrecic.gov.ar\nwww.efili.cancilleria.gov.ar\n\nH.E. DANIEL ANTONIO ROSA\nAmbassador Extraordinary and\nPlenipotentiary\n\nH.E. RICARDO LUIS BOCALANDRO\nAmbassador Extraordinary and\nPlenipotentiary",
