    "body": "Source: B. CURRENT EVENTS - 2025 IN THE PHILIPPINES.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nJanuary\nJanuary 6 - Mervin Guarte (b. 1992), obstacle course racer (Southeast Asian Games\nmultiple medalist)[271]\nJanuary 7 - Deogracias Victor Savellano (b. 1959), undersecretary of the Department of\nAgriculture (since 2023), governor of Ilocos Sur (1992, 2001-2004 and 2007-2010), and\nrepresentative of the 1st district of Ilocos Sur (2016-2022)[272]\nJanuary 25 - Gloria Romero (b. 1933), actress[273]\nJanuary 30:\nSammy Acaylar (b. 1958), volleyball coach (Perpetual Altas, Quezon City Gerflor\nDefenders, men's national team)[274]\nEdcel Lagman (b. 1942), House Minority Leader (2010-2012), representative of the 1st\ndistrict of Albay (1987-1998, 2004-2013 and since 2016), and president of the Liberal\nParty (since 2022)[275]\n\nFebruary\nFebruary 11 - Margarita Forés (b. 1959), chef and restaurateur[276]\n\nTriple K LET Review Solutions\n\nFebruary 14 - Matutina (b. 1946), comedian[277]\nFebruary 25 - Alberto Lina (b. 1948), commissioner of the Bureau of Customs (2015-\n2016)[278]\n\nMarch\nMarch 8 - Oscar Calderon (b. 1951), chief of the Philippine National Police (2006-2007)[279]\nMarch 12 - Eduardo Nonato Joson (b. 1950), governor (1995-1998) and representative of\nthe 1st district of Nueva Ecija (1987-1992 and 2007-2010)[280]\nMarch 15 - Delia Razon (b. 1931), actress[281]\nMarch 16 - Gold Dagal (b. 1986 or 1987), stand-up comedian[282]\nMarch 18 - Edwin Borja (b. 1958), Olympic swimmer (1972, 1976)[283]\nMarch 26 - Estelito Mendoza (b. 1930), solicitor general (1972-1986), Minister of Justice\n(1984-1986) and governor of Pampanga (1985-1986)[284]\nMarch 29 - Virgilio Garcillano (b. 1937), commissioner of the Commission on Elections\n(2004-2005)[285]\n\nApril\nApril 7 - Vicki Brick (b. 1981), basketball player (Maryland Terrapins, women's national\nteam) and businesswoman[286]\nApril 12 - Pilita Corrales (b. 1939), singer and actress[287]\nApril 16 - Nora Aunor (b. 195