eek and Arab\nastronomers. Nonetheless, he\nwas able to demonstrate that\nthese much older observations\nwere more readily explained by\nthe Earth orbiting the Sun rather\n\nCopernicus’s Universe\nThis painting by Andreas Cellarius\nfrom 1660 shows “The system of the\nentire created Universe according\nto Copernicus.”\n\n,\n13 e\nr y erin ted\na\nu\nh\nu\nbr at ec 25)\nFe 42 C d ex 20-\n15 war . 15\nHo rn c\n(bo\n\n42 o\n15 sc\n6, anci\n2\nst Fr\ngu rd a\nt\ne\nAu ania llan ﬁrs ntir\nSp Ore etes of e\nl\ne\nn\nr\nd mp tio ive\nco viga n R\nna azo\nAm\n\n2\n54\n, 1 vier\n2\n6\na\ny\n54\noa\n, 1 an\nMa cis X in G\n28 r Ju at\nn es\na\nr\nFr rriv\nbe lore nds go\na\nla ie\nem xp\npt se e illo an D the t\ne\nS ue abr S ing as\ng\nC\nay or co\nrtu ez t-d xpl n\nPo ríqu sen le e rnia\ni\nd pre wh lifo\nRo\nCa\n\nNatives and llamas were pressed into service to transport silver from Potosí,\nBolivia. The sprawling shanty town became the largest in the New World.\n204\ntons of gold",
