e profoundly relieved\nto have avoided war. Conservative\nMP Winston Churchill (1874-1965)\nwas among the minority who\ndenounced the Munich\nagreement, calling it “a defeat\nwithout a war.”\nPost-Munich optimism only\nlasted until November, when\nKristallnacht (“the Night of\nBroken Glass”) provided graphic\nevidence of the extremist\nnature of the Nazi regime.\n\nSteam record holder\nDesigned by Nigel\nGresley, the steam\nlocomotive\nMallard was\na masterly\nfusion of\nform and\nfunction. It achieved\nan enduring world\nspeed record.\n\nd\nce\nor\nen at\nve ec\ner\nnf ls th t\noti ed r\no\nC ea ep\nom spe\noc\nian ev cc\nh l orld\nEv es r to a iism\ns\ni\n6\nt\ne\nri s w\nly ug nts az\n3 B et\nJu ref wa ng N\nly d s\non one eei\nJ u l l ar\nno ws ﬂ\nMa\nJe\n\nh\nitis\nBr ves k\nr\n4\ni\nee ove\nst rr\ngu on a to s isis s\nu\ni\ne\nr\nA ss\nc\nan\ni\ngu\nm Pra n of erm\nin lutio n G\nso dete\nSu\n\ne, s\n2 s to d tim and\n2\nn m\nr\nie\nbe in ﬂ seco de\nm\ns\nte erla or a s hi\np\nSe amb ny f aise\na\nh\nr\nC rm er\nGe Hitl\nas",
