    "body": "Source: Timelines of History-The Ultimate Visual Guide by Smithsonian.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nIn 1940, Franklin D. Roosevelt\nstood for and won a third term\nin ofﬁce. Before the election,\nRoosevelt had made his hostility\nto Nazi Germany and Japan clear.\nHe had begun rearmament and\nintroduced a measure of\nconscription, but he was\naware of the antiwar\nfeeling among people in\n\nthe US. In a “ﬁreside chat” on\nradio, Roosevelt told Americans\ntheir country was to become the\n“arsenal of democracy,” its\nfactories providing the arms\nfor Britain to ﬁght the Axis.\nall-metal monocoque\nfuselage structure\n\nlaminated wood\npropeller blade\n\nt\ns\nba\ns\nnd\nts\nh ship\nr\nn\nee\n,\ndie d\ne a com\nf\nt\nitis war r,\nn\nf\nm ut\nr\najo rma\ne\naly\na al\nky ate\nrs aig\ni\nt\nr\nB\ni\nI\nM\ns\nh\nb\nw\nb\ne\nn\nt\nF\nt\n3\np\nc\nh\ns\ny\ne\n7\na\n5 Ge\nitl ye, al\nro sin\nuf -sc nd\nly en -K\nnc bl es er\nica cam\nr1 n\nr 2 Jap aty\n3 H da utr\nre em giv ow\n1 T sas lin\n5 L ge gla\nJu k Fr s el\ner\nbe twee RAF\nbe nd Tre\nt 2 , as f Sta\nm d to ar\nr 2 Hen s ne\n0 F Ass ichy al p\nt 1 n lar En\nm\nm\na\ns\ns\n1\ne\nA\ne\nsin Mer a\ne\ne\nd\ne\n,\nw\ne\nb at\ngu ico t o\nly al t V on\ngu egi ern\npt t b an\npt ny rtit\nr 4 nd of\nto\nain\nat geri\nJu tion g a epti\nAu Mex gen\nSe mba ffe\nSe rma ipa\nAu F b outh\nbe ou ut\nOc anco rem\ne Tr\nA s\nAl\nm ee f S o\no twa\nn an a\nr\nNa etin exc\ni\ne\nc\nG\nR\nn\nr\nF\ni\nt\nn\nf\ne\ne\na\np\nitt g U\nm tain\nby\nLu\nsig\nov\nSp\nSe mm pin\nPé\nCo kee\nfor\n\nof\ntle h\nat wit\nB\nF\n10 ins RA e\nly eg n\nh\nJu in b wee er t el\nita et ov nn\nBr es b affe Cha\nsh tw\ncla Luf\nd\nan\n\nGoing underground\nDuring the Blitz, thousands of\nLondoners spent the night in\nUnderground stations to shelter\nfrom the bombing.\n\nish\nr\ns\nrit to\nin\nUS\nas\ntle\nita\n6 B des th\nHi for\n16 ime\n1\nt m raid\nBr rs in\nr\nt eci or s\n2\ns\nt\ns\ns\ns\n1\ne\nn\ne\ne es\nb ce ory\nFir ing don\ngu t d n N an\ner pla