duel\nbetween American and Japanese\naircraft carriers in June 1942.\n\n0\nWARSHIPS\n\nPLANES\n\nAmerican industrial miracle\nThe output of US factories and shipyards soared during World War II.\nThe number of workers employed in shipbuilding alone rose from\naround 100,000 in 1940 to 1.7 million late in the war.\n\nth\nn\nigh of\nea s to th\nh E nce t\nim fall on\ns\nr\ni\na yp\nit\nt C ol t-m\nBr adv Eg\nvie top gh\n27 alts into\nSo vas r ei\ny\nl\n4\nh\nSe fte\nJu my rces\nly\nJu rt of ns a\nAr is fo ein\npo rma\nAx Alam\ne\nG ge\nat\nsie\n\nl\nh s\nra\nUS on\nitis ce\nne s\nt 7 nd\nBr for\nGe take sh\n-\nus s la al\n5\ns\n1\n3\ng\n’\ni\nt 3 r 2 el\nt 1 ry rit\nAu rine lcan\nus be m\nus me f B\nMa ada\nug tem Rom fa\nug tgo d o\nA\nA\nu\nn\ny\nl\nn a\np\ne\nG\nSe puls Ha\nMo mm Arm\nre Alam\nco hth\ng\nat\nEi\n\n3\nr4 s\nr 1 ck r\nbe feat\nbe atta ete\ne\nem y de t\nm\nm\nv\ns\nnc\ni\ne\nra es\nNo rm es a ein\npt orce per\nF\n-\nc\ne\nA\nf\ny\nc\nr\n3\nS is\nh fo\nive ad\nr 2 th for Alam\nVic an\nAx fens ingr\nbe igh is\n11 erm\nto h E s Ax e of\nde Stal\nc\nr\n’\ns\nl\nO iti\nel tt\nbe y G\nof\nBr mm d Ba\nem d b\nov pie\nRo con\nN\nu\nc\nSe\noc\n\nYank tank\nAmerican-built Grant tanks were\nsupplied to the British in North\nAfrica. This one was used by General\nMontgomery as an observation post.\n\nthe city of Stalingrad-of\nsymbolic importance because\nof its name. German soldiers\nentered the city in September,\nbut the Soviets defended it\nstreet-by-street amid the\nruined buildings. In November,\nSoviet General Giorgi Zhukov\n(1896-1974) masterminded a\ncounterattack. Striking from\nnorth and south, his armies\nencircled the Axis forces,\ntrapping a quarter of a million\nmen inside Stalingrad. Ordered\nby Hitler to stay and ﬁght, by\nthe end of the year they were\nstarving, freezing, and short\nof ammunition. The German\ncommander, Field Marshal\nFriedrich Paulus, was among\nthe 90,000 men who lived to\nsurrender the following\nFebruary-and one of only\na handful who then survived\nSoviet imprisonment.\n\n6\nic ved\nr 1 ew r\nom ie\nbe s, N n fo rch\nAt ach ear\nm\n2\no\nr\nn” cl\nve am ose sea\nbe ctio t nu\nNo s Al , ch b re\nem rea ﬁrs ago\nc\nLo xico om\nDe hain ld’s Chic\nMe m b\no\n“c wor r in\nt\na\nat acto\nre",
