    "topic_slug": "social-studies-araling-panlipunan",
    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: MINDGYM SOCIAL STUDIES HUMAN RIGHTS LECTURE NOTES (Part 2)",
    "body": "Source: 2. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-HUMAN RIGHTS_LECTURE NOTES.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n• From the Christian perspectives, the source of\nhuman dignity is rooted in the concept of Christ’s\nredemption and in our ultimate destiny of union\nwith God.\n• Human dignity therefore transcends any social order\nas the basis for rights and is neither granted by\nsociety nor can it be legitimately violated by society.\n• In this way, human dignity is the conceptual basis for\nhuman rights.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nHUMAN DIGNITY &\nHUMAN RIGHTS\n• A violation of a person’s right is a violation of\nhis/her dignity.\n• All persons possess human dignity.\n• The exercise of human dignity flows from the\ndignity of a human person.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nUNIVERSAL DECLARATION\nOF HUMAN RIGHTS\n\n16\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nUNIVERSAL DECLARATION OF\nHUMAN RIGHTS\nHISTORICAL BACKGROUND\n• On December 10, 1948 the General Assembly\nof the United Nations adopted and proclaimed\nthe Universal Declaration of Human Rights.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTHE CONTENT OF THE UDHR\n• Article 1 - \"human beings are born free\nand equal in dignity and rights...\"\n• Articles 2-21 - Civil and political rights\n• Articles 22-29 - Economic and Social\nRights\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSIX CATEGORIES OF RIGHTS\nIN THE UDHR\n1. Security rights protect people against murder,\ninjury, and torture\n2. Due process rights protect people against\narbitrary and excessively harsh punishments,\nand require fair and public trials for those\naccused of crimes.\n\n3. Liberty rights protect people’s freedoms in\nareas such as belief, expression, association,\nand movement.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSIX CATEGORIES OF RIGHTS\nIN THE UDHR\n4. Political rights protect people’s liberty to\nparticipate in politics by assembling,\nprotesting, voting, and serving in public office.\n5. Equality rights guarantee equal citizenship,\nequality before the law, and freedom from\ndiscrimination.\n\n6. Welfare rights require that people be provided\nwith education and protected against\nstarvation and severe poverty.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nFACTS ABOUT THE UDHR\n It is an international bill of rights. It covers all\nof the standard rights, and adds welfare rights.\n It was conceived during World War II as a way\nof creating a safer world and avoiding human\nrights abuses.\n It helped give a fixed meaning to the idea of\nhuman rights by providing an authoritative list.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nThe United Nations\nUniversal Declaration\nof Human Rights\n(UDHR) is the most\nfamous human rights\nagreement in the\nworld. It contains 30\nhuman rights, as seen\non the right.\nAccording to the\nUDHR, you have the\nright to…\n22\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTHE UNITED NATIONS\nCONVENTION ON THE RIGHTS\nOF THE CHILD\n\n23\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nWHO IS A CHILD?\nA child is every human being below the age of 18\nyears unless, national laws recognize the age of\nmajority earlier .\n-CRC, Article 1\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nWHAT ARE THE RIGHTS OF\nTHE CHILD?\n To be born. To have a name and nationality.\n To be free. To have a family who will take care of me.\n To have a good education.\n To develop my potentials.\n To have enough food, shelter, a healthy and active\nbody.\n To be given the opportunity for play and leisure.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nWHAT ARE THE RIGHTS OF\nTHE CHILD?\n To be given protection against abuse, danger and\nviolence brought by war and conflict.\n To be given the opportunity for play and leisure.\n To be given protection against abuse, danger and\nviolence brought by war and conflict.\n To live in a peaceful community.\n To be defended and assisted by the government.\n To be able to express own views.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSurvival Rights\n• Every child has the inherent right to life, and the\nState has an obligation to ensure the child’s\nsurvival and development.\n• They include rights to adequate food, shelter,\nclean water, and primary health care.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDevelopment Rights\n• These are rights to the resources, skills and\ncontributions necessary for the full\ndevelopment of the child.\n• They include rights to formal education, leisure\nand recreation, cultural activities and\ninformation.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nProtection Rights\nThese rights include protection from all forms of\nchild abuse, neglect, exploitation and cruelty,\nincluding the right to special protection in times of\nwar and protection from abuse in the criminal\njustice system.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nBILL OF RIGHTS\n1987 CONSTITUTION\n\n30\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nBILL OF RIGHTS\nSection 1. No person shall be deprived of life,\nliberty, or property without due process of law,\nnor shall any person be denied the equal\nprotection of the laws.\n\nSection 2. The right of the people to be secure in\ntheir persons, houses, papers, and effects against\nunreasonable searches and seizures of whatever\nnature and for any purpose shall be inviolable...\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.",
