    "source_file": "3. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-MAJOR FORMS OF GOVERNMENT_LECTURE NOTES.pdf",
    "source_type": "pdf",
    "source_path": "/Users/lyndon/All reviewers/-LET REVIEWER 2026/C. MAJOR SUBJECTS/F. SOCIAL SCIENCE - SOCIAL STUDIES/MindGym Review Materials/3. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-MAJOR FORMS OF GOVERNMENT_LECTURE NOTES.pdf",
    "exam_scope": "secondary",
    "subject_slug": "major",
    "topic_slug": "social-studies-araling-panlipunan",
    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: MINDGYM SOCIAL STUDIES MAJOR FORMS OF GOVERNMENT LECTURE NOTES (Part 2)",
    "body": "Source: 3. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-MAJOR FORMS OF GOVERNMENT_LECTURE NOTES.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nForms of Government\nB. DICTATORSHIP\n1. Authoritarianism - The political actions and decisions\nof the ruler are not constrained, while political rights\nand freedoms of the citizens are significantly limited.\n2. Totalitarianism - Under this type of regime,\ngovernment uses ideology to captivate people’s\nloyalty to the leader-dictator. The totalitarian dictator\nwields absolute power. The use of coercion, violence\nand force is a tool to maintain obedience from the\npeople.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nForms of Government\nB. DICTATORSHIP\nCharacteristics of Totalitarianism\n−\n\nAs a form of government the totalitarian dictatorship is built\non an ideological foundation. Government utilizes ideology to\ncaptivate the people’s belief and loyalty to the leader-dictator.\nA totalitarian leader wields absolute power.\n\n−\n\nThe use of force, violent coercion and terrorism to control the\npeople.\n\n−\n\nCentralized control by the government of the nation’s\neconomy. Everyone must conform and accept the policies of\nthe dictatorship.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nForms of Government\nB. DICTATORSHIP\nCharacteristics of Totalitarianism\n−\n\nTo maximize the effectiveness of terror as a means of mass\ncontrol, the government controls all means of communication\nand propaganda (eg. Soviet Union)\n\n−\n\nTotalitarianism is also centralized control by the government’s\neconomy. Every business enterprise is regulated, coordinated\nby the existing regime.\n\n−\n\nExamples: Nazism - Adolf Hitler, Fascism - Benito Mussolini,\nChinese Communism - Mao Tze Tung\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nForms of Government\nII. Ruled by the Few\nA. ARISTOCRACY\nDerived from the Greek etymology “Aristo” which\nmeans the “best” and “Kratia or Kratos” which means\nrule. A government by the “best members of the\ncommunity. Aristocrats are presumably men of the\nhighest intelligence and integrity. They belong to the\nelite in society. Their social status, wealth and political\npower are inherited.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nForms of Government\nII. Ruled by the Few\nB. OLIGARCHY\nThis is also a government of a wealthy few but they do\nnot come from nobility like aristocrats. Oligarchs\nbelieve that the most important requisites to claim of\npower are wealth, good social positions and education;\nit is unlikely that oligarchy could serve the interest of\nthe masses since they use their positions in the\ngovernment for their personal benefit. They build\neconomic empires for themselves and their family.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nForms of Government\nIII. Ruled by Many\nDEMOCRACY\n“Demos” derived from the Greek term for people\nand “kratos” which means rule. The Constitution\nguarantees freedom of speech, freedom of\nassociation, freedom of religion and freedom of\nexpression.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nForms of Government\nIII. Ruled by Many\nTwo essential features of Democracy:\n1. Majority Rule - the majority of citizens choose their\nleaders who then have the mandate to govern and\nmake public policies.\n2. Minority Rights - This is ensured so long as the\nminority of citizens openly attempts to win majority\nsupport for leaders and policies without loss of\nindividual rights just as the majority enjoys these\nrights.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nForms of Government\nIII. Ruled by Many\nA democracy is made to work when the following interact:\n1.\n\nCitizens - Active participation of the citizenry is necessary in order to\nprevent government from committing abuses. Citizens can help to balance\nbetween power and authority of government officials. Citizens should\nexercise their freedom and rights within the bounds of the Constitution\nand the law, just as government should exercise its authority within limits.\n\n2.\n\nSuffrage and the Electoral Process - Suffrage is the right conferred by law\nupon a qualified group of citizens to choose their public officials and to\nparticipate in the determination of proposed policies whenever these\npolicies are submitted to them for approval. The citizens must use this right\nto elect qualified people who can govern competently and responsibly.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nForms of Government\nIII. Ruled by Many\nA democracy is made to work when the following interact:\n3.\n\nPolitical Parties - Intertwined with democratic government, this is a group\nof officials or would-be officials who are linked with a sizable group of\ncitizens into an organization; a chief object of this organization is to ensure\nthat its officials attain power or are maintained in power. The party’s nature\nas a structure, tying together a large group of officials and citizens, provides\nan avenue by which one part may control or communicate with another. It\nis this that has made it such a versatile tool of modern politics.\n\n4.\n\nInterest Groups - is an organized group of citizens one of whose goals is to\nensure that the state follows. They aim to represent public opinion and\nhaving it heard in an organized and effective way to government\nauthorities.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nAutocracy\n• A single person holds power.\n• Power is usually inherited or kept by force, i.e.\ndictatorships and monarchies.\n• Government by a single person having\nunlimited power; despotism (domination\nthrough threat of punishment and violence)\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nOligarchy\n• A few individuals hold power.\n• Wealth and military power usually influence\nwho the oligarchs will be.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDemocracy\n• Government is elected by the people.\n• A democracy is determined either directly or\nthrough elected representatives.",
    "material_type": "notes",
    "is_premium": false
  },
