    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: MINDGYM SOCIAL STUDIES PHILIPPINE HISTORY LECTURE NOTES (Part 3)",
    "body": "Source: 4. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-PHILIPPINE HISTORY_LECTURE NOTES.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nJapanese Colonization\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nJAPANESE COLONIZATION\n•\n\n1941, Dec 8. Immediately after the bombing of Pearl\nHarbor, Japanese fighter planes attack the Philippines\nas an ally of the US, shocking the unprepared US and\nFilipino troops. Douglas MacArthur, the Commander\nof the US Armed Forces in the Far East, decides to\nretreat to the Bataan peninsula.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nJAPANESE COLONIZATION\n•\n\n1942, Apr 9. Bataan, under US commander General\nEdward King, is the last province that surrenders to the\nJapanese armies. The infamous Death March follows,\nthe painful trek of 36,000 US and Filipino soldiers and\nguerillas without food and water. Prisoners of war are\nbayonetted or brutally beaten to death by their guards.\nThose who reach San Fernando, Pampanga, are taken\nto a concentration camp at Capaz, Tarlac.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nJAPANESE COLONIZATION\n•\n\n1943, Jun 20. Japanese Premier Hideki Tojo nominates\nan all Filipino 20 member Preparatory Commission\nfor Philippine Independence.\n\n•\n\n1943, Sep 4. The Commission drafts a new\nConstitution which provides for a unicameral national\nassembly.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nJAPANESE COLONIZATION\n•\n\n1943, Sep 20. The 108 delegates to the National\nAssembly are chosen by the members of the\nPreparatory Commission for Philippine Independence.\n\n•\n\n1943, Sep 15. The members of the National Assembly\nelect Jose P. Laurel as the President of the Philippines.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nJAPANESE COLONIZATION\n•\n\n1945, Aug 9. The Americans drop an atomic bomb\nover Nagasaki, Japan.\n\n•\n\n1945, Aug 15. Japan accepts defeat.\n\n•\n\n1946, Jul 4. The US declares the Independence of the\nPhilippines.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nPROPAGANDA MOVEMENT\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDEFECT OF SPANISH COLONIAL RULE\nNo stability in Philippine Government\n• Frequent changes in the government of\nSpain brought also political instability in the\nPhilippines\n• From 1837-1897, the Philippines was ruled\nby 50 Spanish governor generals, each\nserving an average of 1 year and 3 months in\noffice.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDEFECT OF SPANISH COLONIAL RULE\nFilipinos were not given a voice in their own\ngovernment.\n•\n\nTheir previous representation in the Spanish Cortes\n(law making body in Spain) from 1810-1837, was not\nrestored.\n\n•\n\nOnly minor government offices were opened to the\nFilipinos\n\n•\n\nVentura de los Reyes the only Filipino who\nbecame part of the Spanish Cortes in 1812.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDEFECT OF SPANISH COLONIAL RULE\nDefective administration of Justice\n• Courts were really courts of injustice.\n• Spanish judges were ignorant and dishonest\n\n• Judicial trials were slow and expensive\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDEFECT OF SPANISH COLONIAL RULE\nNo equality before the law\n• Spaniards were given more rights and\nprivilege that Filipinos\n\n• Justice was for the rich and influential and\nnot for the poor.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDEFECT OF SPANISH COLONIAL RULE\nMany Spanish officials were corrupt, abusive,\nand incompetent.\n\n• Filipinos were maltreated and regarded as\ninferior beings.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nRISE OF PROPAGANDA\nMOVEMENT\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nRISE OF PROPAGANDA\nMOVEMENT\n•\n\nThe Propaganda Movement was a peaceful crusade\nfor reforms but not a revolutionary movement.\n\n•\n\nIt began in 1872\nended in 1892, when Rizal was exiled to Dapitan.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nAIMS OF PROPAGANDA\nMOVEMENT\n•\n\nEquality of Filipinos and Spaniards before the law.\n\n•\n\nAssimilation of the Philippines as a regular province of\nSpain.\n\n•\n\nRestoration of Philippine representation in the Spanish\nCortes.\n\n•\n\nFilipinization of the parishes\n\n•\n\nGranting of individual liberties to Filipinos such as:\nFreedom of Speech, Freedom of the press, Freedom\nof assembly, Freedom to petition for grievances\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSUPPORTERS OF PROPAGANDA\nMOVEMENT\n•\n\nFerdinand Blumentritt\nin Ateneo de Leitmeritz, Austria\n\n•\n\nMiguel Morayta\nCentral de Madrid\n\n•\n\nFrancisco Pi y Margall former president of the First\nSpanish Republic\n\n•\n\nManuel Ruiz Zorrilla leader of the Republican Party\nof Spain\n\n•\n\nDon Juan de Atayde Spanish writer\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTHE PROPAGANDISTS\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTHE PROPAGANDISTS\nGRACIANO LOPEZ-JAENA\n\nLawyer-journalist from\nBulacan.\nHe was considered as\nthe best propagandist,\neven better than Rizal.\n\nJOSE PROTACIO RIZAL\n\n•\n\n•\n\nThe Great Malayan\nA physician from\nCalamba, Laguna.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTHE PROPAGANDISTS\nMARCELO H. DEL PILAR\n\nOrator of the\npropaganda\nmovement\nA physician from Jaro,\nIloilo\n\nMARIANO PONCE\n\n•\n•\n\nA journalist and\nhistorical researcher\nA physician from\nBaliwag, Bulacan.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2014 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTHE PROPAGANDISTS\nJUAN LUNA",
