    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: MINDGYM SOCIAL STUDIES SOCIETY AND CULTURE LECTURE NOTES (Part 1)",
    "body": "Source: 6. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-SOCIETY AND CULTURE_LECTURE NOTES.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nGENERAL EDUCATION\nSOCIAL STUDIES\n\nCULTURE & SOCIETY\n1\n\n1\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSOCIETY\n A distinct and relatively autonomous\ncommunity whose members' mutual social\nrelations are embedded in and expressed\nthrough the medium of culture.'\n Any portion of a community regarded as a unit\ndistinguishable by particular aims or standards\nof living or conduct'. i.e. culture\n A group of people who occupy a specific\nlocality and who share the same cultural\ntraditions or culture.'\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSOCIAL PARADIGMS\n• Theory: a systematic explanation of how two or\nmore phenomena are related\n• Paradigm: a set of fundamental assumptions that\nguides thinking\n• Sociological imagination (C. Wright Mills)\n• Examining personal experiences in the\ncontext of the larger social structure\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSTRUCTURAL-FUNCTIONALISM\nFocus - balance in societies\nBasics\n Views society as a complex system with many\ninterdependent parts\n Parts work together to promote social stability and\norder; system seeks to maintain equilibrium\n• Function\n Consequences of a given social pattern\n Either manifest or latent\n A macro-oriented (large-scale) paradigm\n•\n•\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nCONFLICT PERSPECTIVE\nFocus - Forces that divide people and the resulting\ndomination and exploitation\n• Basics\n Society consists of institutions that dominant groups\nhave established to reinforce their status\n Society = a structured system based on inequality\n Factors such as race, sex, class, and age are linked to\nsocial inequality\n Social conflict between groups over scarce resources\nis the norm\n A macro-oriented paradigm\n•\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSYMBOLIC INTERACTIONISM\n•\n•\n\nFocus - How people interact with one another\nBasics\n Society is the product of everyday interactions\n Social patterns and processes are creations of people\ninteracting with one another\n Communication between individuals that occurs\nthrough symbols\n George Herbert Mead - Symbols are the essence of\nsocial life and are interpreted by other people\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nCULTURE\nThe knowledge, language,\nvalues, customs, and material\nobjects that are passed from\nperson to person and from one\ngeneration to the next in a\nhuman group or society\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nCHARACTERISTICS OF CULTURE\nCulture is learned\n\n Culture is symbolic\n\nCulture is unconscious\n\n Culture is a way of life\n\nCulture is shared\n\n Culture is dynamic\n\nCulture is integrated\n\n Culture is relative\n\n8\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nELEMENTS OF CULTURE\nMaterial Culture\n• The physical or tangible (see, touch) objects that\nmembers of a society make, use, and share\n• Raw Materials → Technology → Stuff\nNon-Material Culture\n• The abstract or intangible human creations of society\nthat influences people’s behavior\n• Language, beliefs, values, rules of behavior, family\npatterns, political systems\nSymbols\n• Anything that meaningfully represents something else\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nELEMENTS OF CULTURE\nLanguage\n•\n\nA set of symbols that expresses ideas and enable\npeople to think and communicate with one another\n\nValues\n\n•\n\nCollective ideas about what is right or wrong, good or\nbad, and desirable or undesirable in a particular culture\n\nNorms\n\n•\n\nEstablished rules of behavior or standards of conduct\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nELEMENTS OF CULTURE\nFolkways\n•\n\nStandards of behavior that are socially approved but not\nmorally significant\n\nMores\n•\n\nNorms of morality\n\nTaboos\n•\n\nSubjects or behaviors absolutely forbidden by a culture\n\nLaws\n•\n\nformal rules enacted by the state\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSUBCULTURE\nA category of people who share distinguishing\nattributes, beliefs, values, and/or norms that set them\napart in some significant manner from the dominant\nculture. (form around common ethnic/religious\nheritage, SES, occupation)\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nCOUNTERCULTURE\n• A group that strongly rejects dominant societal\nvalues and norms and seeks alternative\nlifestyles.\n• Also a subculture\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nWHAT IS DEVIANCE?\n• Any behavior, belief, or condition that violates\nsignificant social norms in the society or group\nin which it occurs.\n• Interestingly - one who is considered “deviant”\nby one category of people may be seen as\n“conformist” in another group.\n\n• It depends on the time, place and context in\nwhich it occurs, and on the people who define\nand apply the norms.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSOCIAL STRUCTURE\n• The organization of social positions and the\ndistribution of people among them\n• Micro level\n• Individual behavior is shaped by statuses and\nroles\n• Status: position in a social structure that\ndetermines where a person fits in a society\n• Role: set of expected behavior patterns,\nobligations and privileges\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSOCIAL STRUCTURE\nMicro level\n• Role conflict - occurs when one is pulled in\ndifferent directions from different statuses\n\n• Role strain - incompatible demands are built\ninto a single status\nMacro level - Social institutions",
    "material_type": "notes",
    "is_premium": false
  },
