    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: MINDGYM SOCIAL STUDIES SOCIETY AND CULTURE LECTURE NOTES (Part 2)",
    "body": "Source: 6. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-SOCIETY AND CULTURE_LECTURE NOTES.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n• Widely accepted, relatively stable clusters of\nroles, statuses and groups that are designed\nto satisfy the basic needs of a society\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSOCIAL STRATIFICATION\n• The division of society into layers, or strata of\npeople who have unequal amounts of scarce\nbut desirable resources\n• Refers to inequality among groups of people,\nnot individuals\n• Social mobility - The movement of people\nfrom one social position to another\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTYPES OF STRATIFICATION\nSYSTEMS\nCaste System\n\nClass System\n\n• social stratification\nbased on ascribed\nstatus.\n\n• social stratification\nbased on achieved\nstatus.\n\n• India and South Africa\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nWHAT IS DIVERSITY?\n• Cultural diversity refers to the wide range of\ncultural differences found between and within\nnations\n• Can be a result of natural circumstances\n(climate, geography) or social circumstances\n(technology or demographics)\n• Societies can be homogeneous or\nheterogeneous\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nETHNOCENTRISM\n• The practice of judging all other cultures by\none’s own culture\n• Based on the assumption that one’s own way\nof life is superior to all others\n\n• Can be positive or negative\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nCULTURAL RELATIVISM\nThe belief that the behaviors and customs of any\nculture must be viewed and analyzed by the\nculture’s own standards or within the context of a\nparticular society’s responses to problems and\nopportunities\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nCULTURAL UNIVERSALS\nCustoms and practices that occur\nacross all societies\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nSOCIALIZATION\n•\n\nThe lifelong process of social interaction through which\nindividuals acquire a self-identity and the physical,\nmental, and social skills needed for survival in society.\n\n•\n\nAll societies socialize their young.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTHE LOOKING GLASS SELF\n• Imagine how your\npersonality and appearance\nlooks to other people\n• How are they judging you?\n\n• Is your self-concept\nfavorable or unfavorable?\n• Cooley - interaction with\nothers is critical for\nsocialization\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nCOMMUNITY\nRELATIONS\n\n25\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nCOMMUNITY RELATIONS\nFerdinand Tonnies\nGemeinschaft and Gesellschaft\n\nEmile Durkheim\nMechanical and Organic Solidarity\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nGEMEINSCHAFT VS GESSELSCHAFT\n• Gemeinschaft (often translated as community)\nis an association in which individuals are\noriented to the large association.\n• Individuals in Gemeinschaft are regulated by\ncommon mores or beliefs.\n• Gemeinschafts are broadly characterized by a\nmoderate division of labor, strong personal\nrelationships, strong families, and relatively\nsimple social institutions.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nGEMEINSCHAFT VS GESSELSCHAFT\n• Gesellschaft (often translated as society).\n• Gesellschaft is maintained through individuals\nacting in their own self interest.\n\n• Emphasizes secondary relationships rather\nthan familial or community ties, and there is\ngenerally less individual loyalty to society.\n• Social cohesion in Gesellschafts typically\nderives from a more elaborate division of labor.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nMECHANICAL SOCIETIES VS\nORGANIC SOCIETIES\n• Mechanical solidarity applies to societies in\nwhich all members have common and shared\nsocial experiences, and special subdivisions\nwithin a society are either absent or weak.\n• Because of this homogeneity, each individual is\ndirectly and equally attached to the society.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nMECHANICAL SOCIETIES VS\nORGANIC SOCIETIES\n• Organic solidarity societies are formed by a\nsystem of different organs, each of which has a\nspecific role.\n\n• Because individuals’ tasks do not cover all\naspects of their survival, they need to depend\non each other to live in the society.\n• They are held together to each other by one\ncentral organ which controls the rest of the\norganism.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDEPENDENCY THEORY\n\n31\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nDEPENDENCY THEORY\n“Dependence is a conditioning situation in which the\neconomies of one group of countries are conditioned\nby the development and expansion of others.”\n• Model of metropolis-satellite exploitation and\nextraction of economic surplus\n\n• Has origins in the colonial eras; the satellites then\nbecome the colonial metropolises\n• Development of the metropolis corresponds to and\nnecessitates the underdevelopment of the satellites\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nGATT & WTO\n\n33\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nGENERAL AGREEMENT ON\nTARIFFS AND TRADE\n• Multilateral agreement established under US\nleadership in 1948\n• Objective is to liberalize trade by eliminating\ntariffs, subsidies, & import quotas\n\n• 19 original members grew to 120\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.",
