    "source_path": "/Users/lyndon/All reviewers/-LET REVIEWER 2026/C. MAJOR SUBJECTS/F. SOCIAL SCIENCE - SOCIAL STUDIES/MindGym Review Materials/6. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-SOCIETY AND CULTURE_LECTURE NOTES.pdf",
    "exam_scope": "secondary",
    "subject_slug": "major",
    "topic_slug": "social-studies-araling-panlipunan",
    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: MINDGYM SOCIAL STUDIES SOCIETY AND CULTURE LECTURE NOTES (Part 3)",
    "body": "Source: 6. MINDGYM_SOCIAL STUDIES-SOCIETY AND CULTURE_LECTURE NOTES.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nWORLD TRADE\nORGANIZATION\nThe WTO was created during the Uruguay Round of\nGATT to police and enforce GATT rules\n• “deals with the rules of trade between nations at a\nglobal or near-global level”\n\nFormation of WTO had an impact on..\n• Agriculture subsidies\n• Applied GATT rules to services and intellectual property\n\n• Strengthened GATT monitoring and enforcement\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nTERMS:\nANTHROPOLOGY\n\n36\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n• Acculturation - culture change resulting from\ncontact between cultures. A process of\nexternal culture change.\n• Adaptation - patterns of behavior which\nenable a culture to cope with its surroundings.\n• Assimilation - when one ethnic group absorbs\nanother, so that the cultural traits of the\nassimilated group become indistinguishable.\n(minority incorporated into the majority)\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n• Acculturation - culture change resulting from\ncontact between cultures. A process of\nexternal culture change.\n• Adaptation - patterns of behavior which\nenable a culture to cope with its surroundings.\n• Assimilation - when one ethnic group absorbs\nanother, so that the cultural traits of the\nassimilated group become indistinguishable.\n(minority incorporated into the majority)\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n•\n\nAttitudes - data that describe how people think,\nbelieve, and feel.\n\n•\n\nBilingual education - teaching a second language\nby relying heavily on the native language of the\nspeaker. The theory is that maintaining a strong\nsense of one's one culture and language is\nnecessary to acquire another language and culture.\n\n•\n\nBureaucracy - government based on a specialized\nset of offices usually hierarchically organized.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n•\n\nCaste system - the ranking of members in a society by\noccupational status and degree of purity or pollution as\ndetermined by their birth.\n\n•\n\nCultural transmission - how culture is passed on\nthrough learning from one generation to another. Also\nreferred to as enculturation or socialization\n\n•\n\nDiscrimination - the act of disqualifying or mistreating\npeople on grounds rationally irrelevant to the situation.\n\n•\n\nDivision of labor - the division of tasks in a society\nbetween women and men, old and young, ability,\nknowledge, experience.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n•\n\nEconomic development - the institutional changes\nmade to promote economic betterment. It is the\nsocial organizational changes made to promote\ngrowth in an economy.\n\n•\n\nEconomic growth - the overall growth in an\neconomy. Gross national product and gross\ndomestic product are the usual measures of\neconomic growth.\n\n•\n\nEnculturation - the process of learning one's own\nculture, also called socialization.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n•\n\nEquality - a measure of how similar people are to\none another. It can be measured quantitatively\nwith such measures as wealth concentration, Gini\ncoefficients, and percentiles.\n\n•\n\nEquity - the institutional arrangements to\npromote equality. Equity is not quantitatively\nmeasured; it is determined by people agreeing that\ntheir institutions are fair.\n\n•\n\nEthics - the principles of conduct governing an\nindividual or group; concerns for what is right or\nwrong, good or bad.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n•\n\nExtended family - a composite family composed of\nother relatives besides the nuclear families.\n\n•\n\nFamily of orientation - nuclear family consisting of\noneself and one’s father, mother and siblings.\n\n•\n\nFamily of procreation - nuclear family consisting of\noneself and one’s spouse and children.\n\n•\n\nGender - socially agreed-upon traits of men and\nwomen.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n•\n\nGross Domestic Product (GDP) - a measure of an\neconomy's economic performance. It is the market\nvalue of all goods and services produced within the\nboundaries of a country.\n\n•\n\nGross National product (GNP) - a measure of an\neconomy's economic performance. It is the market\nvalue of all goods and services produced by the\nresidents of a particular country. It includes the income\nof those residents earned by corporations owned\noverseas and from working abroad.\n\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n• Hidden curriculum - set of unwritten rules of\nbehavior that are taught in schools.\n• Legitimacy - the right to hold and use power,\nusually based on the consent of the governed\n• Multiculturalism - stressing the importance of\ndifferent cultures, races, and ethnicities.\n• Matriarchy - where a mother figure and\nwomen have authority.\n• Patriarchy - where a father figure and males\nhave authority.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n• Polygamy - an individual who has more than\none spouse.\n• Polygyny - a man has more than one wife.\n• Prejudice - categorical like or dislike of a group\nof people based on real or imagined\ncharacteristics.\n• Religion - set of beliefs and practices that\npertain to sacred things among a community\nof believers. (Durkheim: elements - sacred\nobjects, beliefs, rituals and community.\nExclusively for My Review Coach online LET review. Not for redistribution. © 2011 My Review Coach of\n\nPhilippines.\n\nKEY TERMS\n•\n\nQualitative methods - rich descriptions of cultural\nsituations obtained from interviewing, participant\nobservation, and collection of oral and textual materials.\nEthnographies are reports from qualitative research.\n\n•",
