    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: Social Dimensions of Education Q&A Drills (Part 3)",
    "body": "Source: 5. Social Dimensions of Education Q&A Drills.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\ndesignated by religious authorities of the religion to which the children or wards belong,\nwithout additional cost to the Government.”\n25. A researcher narrated: I observe that when there is an English-speaking foreigner\nin class, more often than not, his classmate perceives him to be superior.” To\nwhich Filipino trait does this point?\nA. Friendliness\nB. Colonial Mentality\nC. Hospitality\nD. Lack of Confidence\nAnswer: B. Colonial Mentality. This is against the principle of nationalism which\nfosters loyalty and patriotism. Nationalism develops responsible citizenship and national\nfeeling.\n26. The failure of independent study with most Filipino students may be attributed to\nA. Unpreparedness for schooling\nB. Ambivalence\nC. High degree of independence\nD. High degree of dependence on authority\nAnswer: D. High degree of dependence on authority. Filipinos are very\ndependent on superiors. Thus, independent study is unpopular.\n27. How will you describe the idea of higher education according to Plato?\nA. Designed to train and blend gentle and fierce qualities in the individuals and\ncreate a harmonious person\nB. Trains the suitably gifted so that they may be qualified to assume the role of\nthe ruling class\nC. Makes the soul responsive to the environment\nD. Helps the soul to search for truth which illuminates it\nAnswer: D. Helps the soul to search for truth which illuminated it. This according to\nPlato is his idea of higher education.\n28. What does UNESCO mean?\nA. United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization\nB. United Nations Environmental, Scholar and Cultural Organization\nC. United Nations Educational, School and Civic Organization\nD. United Nations Environmental, Scholar, and Civic Organization\nAnswer: A. United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization. This\nagency of the United Nations aims to promote peace and security in the world by\n\npromoting collaboration among nations through education, science, culture and\ncommunication.\n29. The medium/media if instructions in schools during the Spanish era, was/were\n_____.\nA. The vernacular\nB. English\nC. Spanish\nD. Filipino\nAnswer: C. - During Spanish era, the medium for instruction was Spanish.\n30. The following philosophers are proponents of perennialism, except _____.\nA. Robert Hutchins\nB. Paolo Freire\nC. Mortimer Adler\nD. Greeks\nAnswer: B. Paolo Freire. Robert Hutchins and Mortimer Adler are famous\nproponents of Perennialism, while Paolo Freire is known as a social reconstructionist.\n31. Which among the following should be developed in the curriculum to counteract\nthe growing number of shooting incident in schools abroad?\nA. Inclusion of socio-emotional teaching\nB. Stress idea to compete on oneself rather than with others\nC. Emphasizes on cooperative learning rather that of competition to others\nD. All of the above\nAnswer: D. All of the above. In cases like this, the curriculum should focus more on\nthe emotional (discipline, positive outlook in life, control of emotions and the like) and\nsocial (sense of belongingness, dealing with others as well as one’s responsibility to\nself, others and society, etc.) aspects of the students, in order to avoid instances of\naggression and violence.\n32. Which among the following describes fully the basis of partnership between\ncommunity and school?\nA. Commonality of interest and success\nB. Mutual trust for other’s values and perspective\nC. Admiration of one’s talent and aspirations\nAnswer: B. for a fruitful partnership to grow between community and school,\nmutual trust for one another’s values, perspectives and experiences must be\nmaintained.\n\n33. How can you best describe the philosophy of Confucius?\nA. Moralistic\nC. Egoistic\nB. Humanistic\nD. Idealistic\nAnswer: B. Confucius philosophy is Humanistic. It occupies mainly with Human\nRelationship and Virtues. Thus, his concept of the Yi (Righteousness) and Yen (Human\nHeartedness) are important.\n34. Most countries outside the Philippines observe _____ high school education.\nA. 4 years\nC. 6 years\nB. 5 years\nD. 7 years\nAnswer: C. 6 years. This is commonly observed by countries outside the Philippines\nwhen it comes to high school.\n35. The DECS was changed to DepEd because of this RA.\nA. RA 7722\nC. RA 9155\nB. RA 7796\nD. RA 7836\nAnswer: C. RA 9155. This changed DECS to DepEd and transferred the “sports” to\nPhilippine Sports Commission and “culture” to the National Commission for the Culture\nand Arts.\n36. This diagram shows the different positions in the school structure and the different\nchannels available should a person wish to talk to a superior.\nA. Chain of command\nB. Organizational chart\nC. Officer chart\nD. Plantilla\nAnswer: B. Organizational chart. This is a diagram that shows the different positions\nin the organization and the flow of communication.\n37. Teacher Rochelle affirms that being a teacher is task entrusted to her by this\nworld. She therefore believes that teaching is a _____.\nA. Mission\nC. vocation\nB. Profession\nD. Bread butter\nAnswer: C. - Teaching is always considered a “vocation” or task entrusted by the\nworld.\n38. Which of the following is not a teacher’s responsibility?\nA. Keep school records",
