    "title": "LET Social Studies Major: Social Dimensions of Education Q&A Drills (Part 10)",
    "body": "Source: 5. Social Dimensions of Education Q&A Drills.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n106.\n“the subject matter should help students understand and appreciate\nthemselves as unique individuals who accept complete responsibility for their\nthoughts, feelings and actions.” From which philosophy is this though based?\nA. Perennialism\nC. Existentialism\nB. Essentialism\nD. Progressivism\nAnswer: C. Existentialism. This philosophy is generally defines as a philosophy of\nsubjectivity or self-hood.\n107.\nWhich of the following prepositions is attributed to Plato?\nA. Truth is relative to a particular time and place.\nB. Human beings create their own truth.\nC. Learning is the discovery of truth as latent ideas are brought to consciousness.\nD. Sense perception is the most accurate guide to knowledge.\nAnswer: C. Learning is the discovery of truth as latent ideas are brought to\nconsciousness. Plato as an idealist believes that truth is universal and changeless.\nTruth is in ideas, the world of forms. Human beings discover truth. Hence, sense\nperception is not reliable.\n108.\nIf a teacher employs more cooperative learning in helping students\ndevelop social values, then the teacher is governed by what philosophy?\nA. Essentialism\nC. Existentialism\nB. Perenialism\nD. Progressivism\nAnswer: D. Progressivism. The type of classroom management that will appear in\nprogressivists will be an environment that stimulates or invites participation, involvement\nand the democratic process.\n109.\nIf reality is politically, socially and economically formed, this philosophy is\nbeing followed.\nA. Essentialism\nC. Existentialism\nB. Perennialism\nD. Progressivism\nAnswer: D. Progressivism. The type of classroom management that will appear in\nprogressivists will be an environment that stimulates or invites participation, involvement\nand the democratic process.\n110.\nA theory of philosophy that defines views about the learner, the teacher\nand the school.\nA. Curriculum\nC. Philosophy of Education\nB. Philosophical analysis\nD. Pedagogy\n\nAnswer: C. Philosophy of Education. (Based on the definition of the term philosophy of\neducation by Dean Webb, Arlene Metha and Forbis Jordan)",
