    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE PART 10.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\n\nSOCIAL SCIENCE (Secondary Education) PART 10 2025/2026\nI. Philippine History and Governance\n1. Which law paved the way for the establishment of the Philippine Commonwealth Government?\nA. Tydings-McDuffie Act\nB. Jones Law\nC. Payne-Aldrich Act\nD. Hare-Hawes-Cutting Act\n2. The Ilustrados during the Spanish era were known as:\nA. Revolutionaries from the masses\nB. Educated Filipino elites\nC. Religious missionaries\nD. Spanish officials\n3. The blood compact between Sikatuna and Legazpi was a symbol of:\nA. Spanish colonization\nB. Friendship and alliance\nC. Religious conversion\nD. Trade expansion\n4. The execution of Gomburza inspired:\nA. The Propaganda Movement\nB. The Ilustrado class\nC. The Cry of Balintawak\nD. The First Philippine Republic\n5. The principle of separation of Church and State is found in which article of the 1987 Constitution?\nA. Article II\nB. Article III\nC. Article IV\nD. Article VI\n\nII. World History and Civilization\n6. The Magna Carta of 1215 limited the powers of:\nA. The British Parliament\nB. The Pope\nC. The English King\nD. The Nobles\n7. Which war was sparked by the assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand?\nA. World War I\nB. World War II\nC. Crimean War\nD. Franco-Prussian War\n8. The philosophy of Karl Marx is mainly associated with:\nA. Liberalism\nB. Communism\nC. Capitalism\nD. Fascism\n9. The Enlightenment emphasized:\nA. Faith and divine right\nB. Reason and individual rights\nC. Obedience to rulers\nD. Religious conformity\n10. The League of Nations failed primarily because:\nA. The U.S. did not join\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\nB. It was too powerful\nC. It focused only on Europe\nD. It had too much military\n\nIII. Geography and Environment\n11. The Ring of Fire refers to:\nA. A desert belt\nB. A volcanic and earthquake zone\nC. A rainforest area\nD. A trade route\n12. Which of the following countries is both in Europe and Asia?\nA. Turkey\nB. Egypt\nC. Kazakhstan\nD. A and C\n13. The capital city located on two continents is:\nA. Moscow\nB. Istanbul\nC. Athens\nD. Cairo\n14. The largest archipelago in the world is:\nA. Japan\nB. Philippines\nC. Indonesia\nD. Malaysia\n15. A map that shows land elevation is called a:\nA. Political map\nB. Topographic map\nC. Climate map\nD. Population map\n\nIV. Sociology and Anthropology\n16. The concept of “cultural relativism” suggests that:\nA. Some cultures are superior\nB. Cultures should be understood within their context\nC. All societies are identical\nD. Cultures should be judged by outsiders\n17. Which is a primary group in sociology?\nA. Political party\nB. Family\nC. Corporation\nD. Government\n18. The transmission of culture from one generation to another is called:\nA. Socialization\nB. Enculturation\nC. Acculturation\nD. Assimilation\n19. The concept of “taboos” refers to:\nA. Socially approved behavior\nB. Socially prohibited acts\nC. Legal norms\nD. Religious doctrines\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\n20. A matrilineal society traces descent through:\nA. Both parents\nB. Mother’s line\nC. Father’s line\nD. Eldest sibling\n\nV. Political Science and Governance\n21. The separation of powers aims to prevent:\nA. Political cooperation\nB. Abuse of authority\nC. Judicial review\nD. Administrative delay\n22. The Senate in the Philippines is composed of how many members?\nA. 12\nB. 24\nC. 25\nD. 30\n23. The power of the Supreme Court to declare laws unconstitutional is called:\nA. Judicial activism\nB. Judicial review\nC. Judicial restraint\nD. Appellate power\n24. Local government units derive their power from:\nA. Constitution\nB. Congress\nC. Local Government Code\nD. Department of Interior and Local Government\n25. The right to vote in elections is called:\nA. Suffrage\nB. Franchise\nC. Plebiscite\nD. Referendum\n\nVI. Economics\n26. The law of supply states that as price increases, supply:\nA. Increases\nB. Decreases\nC. Remains the same\nD. Falls sharply\n27. Opportunity cost means:\nA. The cost of production\nB. The value of the next best alternative forgone\nC. The total market value\nD. The marginal profit\n28. Fiscal policy refers to:\nA. Taxation and government spending\nB. Interest rates and money supply\nC. Import and export controls\nD. Wage regulation\n29. A country’s balance of trade is the difference between:\nA. Imports and exports\nB. GDP and GNP\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\nC. Savings and investment\nD. Income and expenditure\n30. Microeconomics focuses on:\nA. National income\nB. Government budgeting\nC. Individual markets and behavior\nD. Global trade\n\nVII. Globalization and Contemporary Issues\n31. Outsourcing is a result of:\nA. Isolationism\nB. Globalization\nC. Nationalism\nD. Protectionism\n32. The digital divide refers to:\nA. Conflict between cultures\nB. Unequal access to technology\nC. Difference in education\nD. Economic inequality only\n33. The Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) replaced which global agenda?\nA. Agenda 21\nB. Millennium Development Goals\nC. Kyoto Protocol\nD. Paris Agreement\n34. The Kyoto Protocol focuses on:\nA. Human rights\nB. Free trade\nC. Climate change and carbon emissions\nD. Global security\n35. Which international organization ensures monetary stability?\nA. WTO\nB. IMF\nC. WHO\nD. UNICEF\n\nVIII. Asian and Philippine Geography\n36. The Banaue Rice Terraces are found in which province?\nA. Benguet\nB. Ifugao\nC. Mountain Province\nD. Kalinga\n37. The highest mountain in the Philippines is:\nA. Mt. Makiling\nB. Mt. Apo\nC. Mt. Pulag\nD. Mt. Mayon\n38. The two monsoons affecting the Philippines are the:\nA. Amihan and Habagat\nB. El Niño and La Niña\nC. Typhoon and Cyclone\nD. None of the above\n39. The longest river in the Philippines is the:\nA. Pasig River\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\nB. Cagayan River\nC. Pampanga River\nD. Agusan River\n40. The Philippines is part of which major region?\nA. South Asia\nB. East Asia\nC. Southeast Asia\nD. Micronesia",
