    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE PART 9.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\n\nSOCIAL SCIENCE (Secondary Education) PART 9 2025/2026\nI. Philippine History and Government\n1. Who is considered the “Father of the Philippine Revolution”?\nA. Jose Rizal\nB. Andres Bonifacio\nC. Emilio Aguinaldo\nD. Apolinario Mabini\n2. The Cry of Pugad Lawin symbolizes:\nA. The first victory of the revolution\nB. The start of the Philippine Revolution\nC. The signing of the Pact of Biak-na-Bato\nD. The declaration of independence\n3. The Malolos Constitution was the first republican constitution in Asia. It was ratified in:\nA. 1896\nB. 1898\nC. 1899\nD. 1901\n4. The first president of the Commonwealth of the Philippines was:\nA. Sergio Osmeña\nB. Manuel L. Quezon\nC. Manuel Roxas\nD. Emilio Aguinaldo\n5. The Katipunan was founded primarily to:\nA. Promote education\nB. Gain independence from Spain\nC. Establish a political party\nD. Support U.S. colonization\n\nII. World History and Civilization\n6. The Renaissance began in which European country?\nA. France\nB. England\nC. Italy\nD. Germany\n7. The Industrial Revolution started in:\nA. Germany\nB. France\nC. England\nD. United States\n8. The Cold War was primarily between:\nA. Germany and France\nB. USA and USSR\nC. China and Japan\nD. Britain and Spain\n9. Who proposed the theory of evolution by natural selection?\nA. Gregor Mendel\nB. Isaac Newton\nC. Charles Darwin\nD. Albert Einstein\n10. The fall of the Berlin Wall in 1989 symbolized:\nA. The beginning of World War II\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\nB. The end of the Cold War\nC. The rise of communism\nD. The start of globalization\n\nIII. Geography and Environment\n11. The imaginary line dividing the Earth into Northern and Southern Hemispheres is the:\nA. Tropic of Cancer\nB. Tropic of Capricorn\nC. Equator\nD. Prime Meridian\n12. Which continent is known as the “Dark Continent”?\nA. Africa\nB. Asia\nC. Europe\nD. Australia\n13. The largest ocean in the world is the:\nA. Atlantic Ocean\nB. Indian Ocean\nC. Pacific Ocean\nD. Arctic Ocean\n14. The Philippines is located within which major climatic zone?\nA. Temperate\nB. Tropical\nC. Polar\nD. Subarctic\n15. The natural boundary between Europe and Asia is the:\nA. Himalayas\nB. Ural Mountains\nC. Alps\nD. Caucasus Mountains\n\nIV. Sociology and Anthropology\n16. The study of human behavior and society is called:\nA. Anthropology\nB. Sociology\nC. Psychology\nD. Political Science\n17. The smallest unit of society is the:\nA. Community\nB. Family\nC. Barangay\nD. Tribe\n18. The concept of “utang na loob” in Filipino culture exemplifies:\nA. Materialism\nB. Reciprocity\nC. Competition\nD. Individualism\n19. Who is known as the “Father of Sociology”?\nA. Max Weber\nB. Auguste Comte\nC. Karl Marx\nD. Emile Durkheim\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\n20. The study of prehistoric humans and their tools is called:\nA. Archaeology\nB. Linguistics\nC. Geography\nD. Sociology\n\nV. Political Science and Governance\n21. The principle that government power comes from the consent of the governed is known as:\nA. Social contract\nB. Separation of powers\nC. Divine right\nD. Checks and balances\n22. The branch of government that interprets laws is the:\nA. Executive\nB. Legislative\nC. Judiciary\nD. Cabinet\n23. The Philippine Constitution guarantees freedom of speech under:\nA. Article II\nB. Article III\nC. Article VI\nD. Article VII\n24. The highest law of the land is the:\nA. Constitution\nB. Civil Code\nC. Bill of Rights\nD. Presidential Decree\n25. The 1987 Constitution was ratified during the term of:\nA. Ferdinand Marcos\nB. Corazon Aquino\nC. Fidel Ramos\nD. Gloria Macapagal-Arroyo\n\nVI. Economics\n26. The basic economic problem of scarcity means:\nA. Resources are unlimited\nB. People have limited wants\nC. Resources are limited, but wants are unlimited\nD. Goods are always abundant\n27. GDP stands for:\nA. Gross Domestic Product\nB. General Domestic Price\nC. Gross Demand Potential\nD. Government Development Plan\n28. Demand law states that as price increases, quantity demanded:\nA. Increases\nB. Decreases\nC. Remains constant\nD. Doubles\n29. A market structure dominated by a single seller is called:\nA. Monopoly\nB. Oligopoly\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\nC. Monopolistic competition\nD. Perfect competition\n30. Inflation is defined as:\nA. A general decrease in prices\nB. A general increase in prices\nC. A stable price level\nD. A controlled economy\n\nVII. Asian and World Geography\n31. The longest river in the world is the:\nA. Amazon\nB. Yangtze\nC. Nile\nD. Mississippi\n32. Mount Everest is located between:\nA. China and India\nB. Nepal and China\nC. India and Pakistan\nD. China and Bhutan\n33. The Great Wall was built to protect China from:\nA. Koreans\nB. Mongols\nC. Japanese\nD. Europeans\n34. The smallest continent in the world is:\nA. Europe\nB. Antarctica\nC. Australia\nD. South America\n35. Which Southeast Asian country was never colonized by Western powers?\nA. Philippines\nB. Indonesia\nC. Thailand\nD. Malaysia\n\nVIII. Current Issues and Globalization\n36. ASEAN stands for:\nA. Association of Southeast Asian Nations\nB. Alliance of South East Asia Network\nC. Asian States Economic Association Nations\nD. Association of South East Asia Neighbors\n37. Globalization is characterized by:\nA. Isolation of economies\nB. Integration of world economies\nC. Rise of protectionism\nD. Decrease in communication\n38. Climate change is mainly caused by:\nA. Volcanic eruptions\nB. Human industrial activity\nC. Earthquakes\nD. Solar flares\n39. The United Nations was established in:\nA. 1919\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\nB. 1945\nC. 1950\nD. 1960\n40. The Universal Declaration of Human Rights was adopted by the UN in:\nA. 1940\nB. 1945\nC. 1948\nD. 1951\n\nIX. Social Studies Pedagogy\n41. The main goal of teaching Social Studies is to:\nA. Memorize historical facts\nB. Develop civic competence\nC. Focus on geography\nD. Learn world languages\n42. The spiral progression approach means:\nA. Students study topics once only\nB. Simple to complex revisiting of themes\nC. Teaching only one subject\nD. Emphasizing rote learning\n43. Using maps and charts in teaching promotes:\nA. Listening skills\nB. Visual learning\nC. Memorization\nD. Writing ability\n44. Which method encourages critical thinking in Social Studies?\nA. Debate\nB. Dictation\nC. Lecture\nD. Recitation\n45. The K-12 Social Studies curriculum emphasizes:\nA. Geography only\nB. Citizenship, values, and cultural understanding\nC. Economic computation\nD. Memorization of events",
