    "body": "Source: SOCIAL SCIENCE PART 9.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nX. Research and Assessment\n46. The first step in conducting historical research is:\nA. Interpretation\nB. Data collection\nC. Identifying the problem\nD. Hypothesis formulation\n47. Primary sources include:\nA. Textbooks\nB. Diaries and letters\nC. Encyclopedias\nD. Biographies\n48. A teacher uses group investigation and role-playing to teach. This is an example of:\nA. Experiential learning\nB. Traditional learning\nC. Drill method\nD. Lecture method\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\n49. The best assessment for a community mapping activity is:\nA. Objective test\nB. Portfolio assessment\nC. Multiple-choice quiz\nD. Oral recitation\n50. The main purpose of authentic assessment is to:\nA. Focus on recall\nB. Measure real-world application\nC. Simplify grading\nD. Limit creativity\n\nUltimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nLearnUP PH Reviewer\nAnswer Key with Short Explanations\n1. Andres Bonifacio - Led the Katipunan.\n2. The start of the revolution - Cry of Pugad Lawin began the revolt.\n3. 1899 - Year Malolos Constitution was ratified.\n4. Manuel L. Quezon - First Commonwealth president.\n5. Gain independence from Spain - Katipunan’s goal.\n6. Italy - Birthplace of Renaissance.\n7. England - Start of Industrial Revolution.\n8. USA and USSR - Cold War rivals.\n9. Charles Darwin - Proposed evolution by natural selection.\n10. The end of the Cold War - Fall of Berlin Wall.\n11. Equator - Divides Earth into hemispheres.\n12. Africa - Called “Dark Continent.”\n13. Pacific Ocean - Largest ocean.\n14. Tropical - Climate zone of the Philippines.\n15. Ural Mountains - Divide Europe and Asia.\n16. Sociology - Study of human society.\n17. Family - Smallest social unit.\n18. Reciprocity - “Utang na loob” shows social obligation.\n19. Auguste Comte - Father of Sociology.\n20. Archaeology - Study of ancient humans.\n21. Social contract - Power from consent of governed.\n22. Judiciary - Interprets laws.\n23. Article III - Bill of Rights.\n24. Constitution - Supreme law.\n25. Corazon Aquino - Ratified 1987 Constitution.\n26. Resources are limited, wants unlimited - Definition of scarcity.\n27. Gross Domestic Product - Total output in an economy.\n28. Decreases - Law of demand.\n29. Monopoly - Single seller.\n30. Increase in prices - Definition of inflation.\n31. Nile - Longest river.\n32. Nepal and China - Location of Everest.\n33. Mongols - Reason for Great Wall’s construction.\n34. Australia - Smallest continent.\n35. Thailand - Never colonized.\n36. Association of Southeast Asian Nations - ASEAN acronym.\n37. Integration of world economies - Essence of globalization.\n38. Human industrial activity - Main cause of climate change.\n39. 1945 - UN establishment.\n40. 1948 - UDHR adoption.\n41. Develop civic competence - Goal of Social Studies.\n42. Simple to complex revisiting - Spiral progression.\n43. Visual learning - Maps aid understanding.\n44. Debate - Encourages critical thinking.\n45. Citizenship and values - K-12 focus.\n46. Identifying the problem - First research step.\n47. Diaries and letters - Primary sources.\n48. Experiential learning - Active, participative learning.\n49. Portfolio assessment - Best for project-based work.\n50. Measure real-world application - Purpose of authentic assessment.",
